E["npc:doctor-gregory-victor"] = {t="npc",n="Doctor Gregory Victor",z="arathi",s="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor tends the Horde’s wounded and trains medics for the fighting in the Arathi Highlands. Renowned as its premier trauma physician, he teaches advanced triage and battlefield first aid.",h="At Hammerfall, Doctor Gregory Victor tends the Horde’s wounded and trains medics for the fighting in the...",sec={{t="Surgeon of Hammerfall",b="Doctor Gregory Victor treats the Horde’s wounded at Hammerfall, in the contested Arathi Highlands. Though many distrust Forsaken apothecaries, he uses surgery instead of blighted alchemy on soldiers hurt by Syndicate brigands, Boulderfist ogres, and Alliance forces. Hammerfall is the Horde’s main proving ground for field medics, and Victor demands speed and care when the most critical patients are under pressure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is a Forsaken physician at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and the Horde’s premier trauma surgeon. He oversees triage and trains advanced field medics.",al={"doctor victor","gregory victor","who is gregory victor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Doctor Gregory Victor?",a="You can find Doctor Gregory Victor inside Hammerfall, in northeastern Arathi Highlands.",al={"gregory victor location","where is victor","doctor victor where"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does he play for the Horde?",a="Doctor Victor tests promising field medics in battlefield triage. He teaches them to stabilize the dying and make advanced cloth bandages for frontline combat.",al={"what does gregory victor do","gregory victor first aid","horde trauma doctor"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is his Alliance counterpart?",a="Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen is the Alliance counterpart. He oversees advanced trauma and triage training at Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"alliance equivalent doctor victor","alliance triage doctor"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Doctor Gregory Victor on?",a="Doctor Gregory Victor is loyal to the Horde and the Forsaken. Stationed out at Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, he serves as an expert surgeon attending to the faction's wounded and passing on advanced triage knowledge to those willing to learn.",al={"what faction is gregory victor","is doctor victor horde","doctor victor allegiance"},it="side",add="d46fa605"},{q="What does Doctor Gregory Victor want?",a="Doctor Victor is dedicated to field medicine and surgery. He seeks capable battlefield medics who can handle high-pressure triage, testing aspiring healers to ensure they can prioritize treatments and save lives amid the chaos of war.",al={"what does doctor victor want","doctor gregory victor goals","what is victor doing"},it="wants",add="5e053b25"},{q="Why is Doctor Gregory Victor here?",a="Doctor Victor is stationed in Hammerfall to support the Horde's front lines in the contested Arathi Highlands. With constant skirmishes erupting against the Alliance and local threats, an experienced trauma surgeon is essential to keep soldiers alive.",al={"why is gregory victor here","why is doctor victor in hammerfall","reason victor is here"},it="why_here",add="3e1305a9"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Doctor Victor for battlefield medicine at a precarious outpost. He helps warriors on the Arathi front return to fighting shape.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you can see Doctor Victor’s work as proof that the Forsaken can master mortal anatomy and restorative surgery, apart from the Royal Apothecary Society’s toxic concoctions."},kw={"arathi highlands","doctor gregory victor","first aid","gregory victor","hammerfall","horde trauma","surgeon","triage"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","quest:6623","zone:arathi","npc:doctor-gustaf-vanhowzen","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Doctor Gregory Victor"}}
E["npc:orgrim-doomhammer"] = {t="npc",n="Orgrim Doomhammer",z="arathi",s="During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer led the Old Horde as its supreme Warchief. He became one of history’s greatest orc warriors. He died freeing the internment camps in the Arathi Highlands, but his legacy lives on in Orgrimmar and through Thrall, who inherited his warhammer and black plate armor.",h="During the Second War, Orgrim Doomhammer led the Old Horde as its supreme Warchief.",sec={{t="Rise of the Warchief",b="Orgrim Doomhammer rose from second-in-command to become Chieftain of the Blackrock clan. Gul'dan offered him demonic blood, but Orgrim refused and kept his doubts hidden beneath fierce loyalty. Near the end of the First War, he turned against the Shadow Council after its treachery and the murder of his childhood friend Durotan.\n\nOrgrim slew Blackhand in honorable combat and took the mantle of Warchief. He purged Gul'dan's warlocks and led the Horde across the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War. A devastating strategist, he drove human kingdoms to the brink of ruin. Gul'dan's betrayal split his forces, and Orgrim was defeated and captured outside Blackrock Spire.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Legacy",b="Orgrim Doomhammer escaped human captivity and lived in hiding until he met Thrall, Durotan's orphaned son. The young shaman's vision gave Orgrim new purpose, and he rallied the remaining orcish clans to storm the internment camps and free their people.\n\nDuring a fierce battle at an encampment in the Arathi Highlands, a lance struck the Warchief from behind. As he lay dying, Orgrim gave Thrall his black plate armor, his ancestral weapon, the Doomhammer, and the title of Warchief. The liberated outpost was renamed Hammerfall in his honor, and the newly founded capital in Durotar was named Orgrimmar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Orgrim Doomhammer?",a="Orgrim Doomhammer was Chieftain of the Blackrock clan and Warchief of the Horde during the Second War. After escaping human captivity, he fought beside Thrall to free their imprisoned kin and died in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who is doomhammer","orgrim doomhammer background","who was warchief doomhammer"}},{q="How did Orgrim Doomhammer die?",a="Orgrim Doomhammer was struck from behind by a knight's lance during an assault on a human internment camp in the Arathi Highlands. Thrall took up his mantle, and the site was named Hammerfall in his memory.",al={"orgrim doomhammer death","how did doomhammer die","who killed doomhammer"}},{q="Why is the Horde capital named Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall named the fortified city in Durotar for Orgrim Doomhammer, his mentor and predecessor. Orgrim saw promise in Thrall and named him the new Warchief, so the Horde could rebuild on honor rather than demonic corruption.",al={"why is it called orgrimmar","orgrimmar namesake","city named after orgrim"}},{q="Did Orgrim drink the demon blood?",a="No. Orgrim Doomhammer refused the demonic blood and concealed his doubts behind loyalty to Blackhand. He later destroyed Gul'dan's Shadow Council from within.",al={"did doomhammer drink blood","was orgrim corrupted","orgrim demon blood"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you revere Orgrim Doomhammer for freeing your people from lethargy and internment. He chose honor over demonic subjugation.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, Orgrim Doomhammer remains a grim symbol of how close the Eastern Kingdoms came to ruin during the Second War. He butchered countless champions before his defeat at Blackrock Spire."},kw={"blackhand","blackrock","doomhammer","hammerfall","orgrim","orgrimmar","thrall","warchief"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:orgrimmar","zone:arathi","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:old-horde","topic:second-war","topic:first-war","topic:horde"},src={"Orgrim Doomhammer"}}
E["npc:skuerto"] = {t="npc",n="Skuerto",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto scouts the dangerous Arathi Highlands for the Alliance. Archmage Malin sent him with Apprentice Kryten to gather arcane reagents and recover artifacts once owned by Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto scouts the dangerous Arathi Highlands for the Alliance.",sec={{t="A Scout in the Highlands",b="Skuerto scouts the dangerous Arathi Highlands for the Alliance. The Ironforge dwarf is stationed at Refuge Pointe with Apprentice Kryten. Archmage Malin directs their search for arcane reagents and powerful artifacts once owned by his old master, Archmage Trelane.",sp=0},{t="Pride and Peril",b="Skuerto takes pride in scouting the harsh Highlands and bristles when anyone questions his skill. His work brings him near the region's dangers: the hostile Syndicate, Boulderfist ogres, and ancient entities bound to the land.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Skuerto stationed in Arathi instead of Ironforge?",a="Archmage Malin sent Skuerto to Refuge Pointe with Apprentice Kryten. They gather reagents and recover items left behind by Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane, who fled Stromgarde when it fell under siege.",al={"why is skuerto here","skuerto backstory"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Skuerto's mission at Refuge Pointe?",a="Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten gather arcane reagents and recover powerful magical artifacts once owned by Archmage Trelane, Malin's former master.",al={"skuerto purpose","what does skuerto do","skuerto malin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are Skuerto's allies in the region?",a="Skuerto works with Apprentice Kryten, his partner in Archmage Malin's work, and with the Alliance defenders holding Refuge Pointe.",al={"skuerto friends"},it="allies"},{q="Who is Skuerto?",a="Skuerto is an Ironforge dwarf scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Proud of his reconnaissance skills and notably sensitive to criticism, he operates in the field alongside Apprentice Kryten on behalf of the Alliance.",al={"who is skuerto","skuerto identity","who is the dwarf skuerto"},it="identity",add="9a7bedf3"},{q="Whose side is Skuerto on?",a="Skuerto is firmly loyal to the Alliance and Ironforge. Operating out of the Alliance encampment at Refuge Pointe, he works in coordination with Dalaran mages and local Alliance forces against the threats looming over the Arathi Highlands.",al={"skuerto faction","is skuerto alliance","skuerto allegiances"},it="side",add="1cc8a254"},{q="What does Skuerto want?",a="Skuerto wants to fulfill the mission given to him by Archmage Malin: securing magical reagents and reclaiming powerful lost artifacts that once belonged to Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane, all while defending his reputation as a capable scout.",al={"what does skuerto want","skuerto goals","skuerto motives"},it="wants",add="5f13d7e3"},{q="Who is Skuerto tied to?",a="Beyond working under Archmage Malin and alongside Apprentice Kryten, Skuerto stands with the Alliance defenders holding Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"skuerto ties","skuerto connections","who does skuerto know"},it="ties",add="44066d31"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, Skuerto shows the grit of those serving the Alliance on its wild frontiers. His scout's pride is easily bruised."},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","ironforge","refuge pointe","scout","skuerto","trelane"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","zone:ironforge","topic:alliance"},src={"Skuerto"}}
E["quest:635"] = {t="quest",n="Crystal in the Mountains",z="arathi",s="In Arathi's northern mountains, a vision draws you toward a gleaming crystal. The Pendant of Myzrael pulses in your hand as a plea for help reaches you.",h="In Arathi's northern mountains, a vision draws you toward a gleaming crystal.",sec={{t="A Silent Plea",b="The Pendant of Myzrael pulses in your hand, carrying a plea from someone in need of help. Then a vision shows a gleaming crystal thrusting from the ground in the mountains north of Arathi. You feel drawn there.",sp=0},{t="At the Crystal",b="At the crystal, its pulse suggests a living force is trapped within.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What starts this journey?",a="The Pendant of Myzrael begins this journey. As you hold it, it pulses with a plea from someone in desperate need of help.",al={"how to get crystal in the mountains","where does pendant of myzrael come from","crystal in the mountains start"}},{q="Where does the vision lead?",a="The vision leads you to a gleaming crystal in Arathi's northern mountains. You feel drawn there.",al={"where is the crystal","crystal in the mountains location","find the crystal from vision"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","crystal","crystal in the mountains","pendant of myzrael","shards of myzrael","vision"},rel={"zone:arathi"},m={start="Pendant of Myzrael",["end"]="Shards of Myzrael",level="35",id=635},src={"Crystal in the Mountains"}}
E["quest:639"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Strom",z="arathi",s="At Hammerfall, Zengu seeks the sigils that guard Trol'kalar, Lord Ignaeus Trollbane's sword. The Syndicate took the Sigil of Strom, and one of its agents in Stromgarde likely carries it.",h="At Hammerfall, Zengu seeks the sigils that guard Trol'kalar, Lord Ignaeus Trollbane's sword.",sec={{t="The Legacy of Trollbane",b="Long ago, Lord Ignaeus of Strom, called Trollbane, was the Arathorian Empire's ablest foe in its war against the trolls. He wielded Trol'kalar in battle. In the trolls' old tongue, its name means troll slayer. Now Trollbane's sons are weakened, and their stronghold lies in ruins.",sp=0},{t="The First Sigil",b="Several sigils guard Trol'kalar, and Stromgarde's survivors each took some. Zengu says they must all be recovered. The Syndicate seized the first, the Sigil of Strom. Zengu believes one of its agents in Stromgarde holds it. Bring the sigil back to Zengu at Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zengu?",a="At Hammerfall in Arathi, Zengu is gathering the sigils that guard Trol'kalar, Lord Ignaeus Trollbane's sword.",al={"who gives sigil of strom","zengu hammerfall"}},{q="What is Trol'kalar?",a="Trol'kalar means troll slayer in the trolls' ancient tongue. Lord Ignaeus of Strom, called Trollbane, rode into battle against the trolls with the sword.",al={"what is trolkalar","trol'kalar meaning","trollbane sword"}},{q="Why is the Sigil of Strom needed?",a="Several sigils guard Trol'kalar, and Stromgarde's survivors divided them among themselves. Zengu wants them all, beginning with the Sigil of Strom.",al={"why get the sigil","purpose of sigil of strom"}},{q="Who holds the Sigil of Strom?",a="The Syndicate took the Sigil of Strom. One of its agents in Stromgarde is most likely carrying it.",al={"who has the sigil of strom","where is the sigil of strom","syndicate sigil"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","ignaeus","sigil of strom","stromgarde","syndicate","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu"},rel={"quest:638","quest:640","quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","topic:syndicate","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="37",faction="Horde",id=639},src={"Sigil of Strom (Classic)"}}
E["quest:640"] = {t="quest",n="The Broken Sigil",z="arathi",s="Zengu sends you to recover sigils from the Stromgarde militia. Galen, son of Thoras Trollbane, broke the Sigil of Thoradin into eleven pieces, and you carry them to Tor'gan in Hammerfall.",h="Zengu sends you to recover sigils from the Stromgarde militia.",sec={{t="A Sigil in Pieces",b="Three sigils guard Thoras Trollbane's tomb. You have taken the first from the Syndicate. The firmly entrenched Stromgarde militia holds the other two. Galen, Thoras' son, broke the Sigil of Thoradin into eleven pieces and scattered them among the defenders.",sp=0},{t="To Tor'gan",b="Zengu asks you to gather the pieces from Stromgarde's defenders. Then carry them to Tor'gan, the troll shaman at Hammerfall. He can bind them into a whole sigil.",sp=0},{t="At Hammerfall",b="Tor'gan says Zengu told him you needed help. He examines the pieces and judges the work manageable. All eleven are present, and the sigil's magical structure is easy to restore. Tor'gan tells you to close your eyes. Soon, he declares the Sigil of Thoradin whole again.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Sigil of Thoradin?",a="The Sigil of Thoradin is one of three sigils guarding Thoras Trollbane's tomb. Galen broke it into eleven pieces and scattered them among Stromgarde's defenders.",al={"sigil of thoradin lore","broken sigil meaning","what is the broken sigil"}},{q="Who divided the sigil?",a="Galen, son of Thoras Trollbane, broke the Sigil of Thoradin into eleven pieces and scattered them among Stromgarde's defenders.",al={"who broke the sigil","why is the sigil broken","galen trollbane sigil"}},{q="Where are the sigil fragments held?",a="Stromgarde's defenders hold the pieces among the firmly entrenched militia guarding the remaining sigils.",al={"where to find fragments","who has the fragments","stromgarde defenders sigil"}},{q="Who can bind the broken sigil?",a="Tor'gan, the troll shaman at Hammerfall, can bind the pieces into a whole sigil.",al={"who fixes the sigil","torgan sigil","who binds the fragments"}},{q="What came before this?",a="It follows Sigil of Strom, where you recovered the first sigil from the Syndicate.",al={"previous quest","what quest comes before the broken sigil","sigil chain start"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","broken sigil","galen trollbane","hammerfall","sigil of thoradin","stromgarde","thoras trollbane","tor'gan","zengu"},rel={"quest:641","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:645","topic:shaman","topic:syndicate","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="40",faction="Horde",id=640},src={"The Broken Sigil"}}
E["quest:641"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Thoradin",z="arathi",s="Tor'gan has restored the Sigil of Thoradin, and Zengu waits in Hammerfall for its return. The sigil can open the seal on Trollbane's tomb.",h="Tor'gan has restored the Sigil of Thoradin, and Zengu waits in Hammerfall for its return.",sec={{t="The Restored Sigil",b="Tor'gan's reconstruction has worked. The Sigil of Thoradin can open the seal on Trollbane's tomb, so he sends you back to Zengu in Hammerfall. Zengu has more for you to do.",sp=0},{t="Halfway There",b="Zengu asks whether you have the second sigil. With it, he says, you are halfway to taking Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb. The third sigil remains hard to find because its keepers move about Arathi. Zengu trusts you will find it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Sigil of Thoradin used for?",a="The restored sigil can open the seal on Trollbane's tomb.",al={"sigil of thoradin purpose","what does sigil of thoradin do","why do we need the sigil"}},{q="Who do you bring the Sigil of Thoradin to?",a="Bring the restored sigil to Zengu in Hammerfall. Tor'gan sends you back to him.",al={"where do i take the sigil","who turns in sigil of thoradin","sigil of thoradin turn in"}},{q="Where does this step fit in the search for Trol'kalar?",a="This step follows The Broken Sigil, when Tor'gan reconstructed the sigil from the pieces you brought him.",al={"sigil chain progress","how far along is this quest","what quest is before this"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","sigil of thoradin","tor'gan","trol'kalar","trollbane's tomb","zengu"},rel={"quest:640","quest:645","quest:638","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Zengu",level="40",faction="Horde",id=641},src={"Sigil of Thoradin (Classic)"}}
E["quest:643"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Arathor",z="arathi",s="Zengu sends you from Hammerfall to seek a sigil carried by human cavalry in the Arathi Highlands. Find their leader, Lieutenant Valorcall, and bring the sigil back.",h="Zengu sends you from Hammerfall to seek a sigil carried by human cavalry in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="The Prince's Cavalry",b="Zengu doubts the humans can claim Stromgarde, much less the whole Arathi Highlands. Yet their prince still sends the last of his horsemen through the countryside. Zengu cannot see why. He knows Lieutenant Valorcall leads those riders and carries one of the sigils. Find Valorcall and bring it back to Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="On Horseback",b="Zengu warns that Valorcall is hard to catch, for his horse bears him swiftly across the land. If Valorcall is gone, Stromgarde's defenders will suffer a heavy blow. Then the Horde will stand one sigil away from claiming Trol'kalar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to find the Sigil of Arathor?",a="Zengu sends you from Hammerfall to find the Sigil of Arathor.",al={"sigil of arathor quest giver","who gives sigil of arathor","where to get sigil of arathor"}},{q="Who holds the Sigil of Arathor?",a="Lieutenant Valorcall leads the human cavalry and holds the Sigil of Arathor. The human prince gave it to him, and Zengu says Valorcall rides on horseback and is hard to track.",al={"who has the sigil of arathor","where is valorcall","lieutenant valorcall location"}},{q="Why does Lieutenant Valorcall have the sigil?",a="Zengu says the human prince gave one of the sigils to Lieutenant Valorcall, but he does not say why.",al={"why does valorcall have the sigil","who gave valorcall the sigil"}},{q="Where does this fit in the Trol'kalar chain?",a="The Sigil of Arathor is the fifth step in the Trol'kalar chain. It follows the Sigil of Thoradin, and the Sigil of Trollbane comes next.",al={"trolkalar quest chain arathor","what comes before sigil of arathor","what comes after sigil of arathor"}},{q="Where do you bring the sigil once it is found?",a="Bring the sigil back to Zengu in Hammerfall.",al={"where to turn in sigil of arathor","sigil of arathor turn in"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","lieutenant valorcall","sigil of arathor","stromgarde","trol'kalar","valorcall","zengu"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:645","topic:human"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="41",faction="Horde",id=643},src={"Sigil of Arathor (Classic)"}}
E["quest:644"] = {t="quest",n="Sigil of Trollbane",z="arathi",s="In Hammerfall, Zengu sends you deep into Stromgarde for the Sigil of Trollbane. Prince Galen keeps the last sigil, which is needed to claim Trol'kalar.",h="In Hammerfall, Zengu sends you deep into Stromgarde for the Sigil of Trollbane.",sec={{t="The Last Sigil",b="Prince Galen, son of Thoras Trollbane, keeps the last sigil in Stromgarde. He waits in a chapel deep in the districts held by the militia. Zengu warns that Galen is well guarded and a fine fighter. You are to kill the prince and carry the sigil back to Zengu in Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Zengu's Verdict",b="Zengu asks whether the line of Ignaeus Trollbane is broken. When it is, he declares that Trollbane blood will no longer haunt his people. They now hold every sigil needed to claim Trol'kalar. Zengu vows they will soon strike at the trolls of Zul'Gurub, whom he hates.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to retrieve the Sigil of Trollbane?",a="Zengu sends you from Hammerfall to retrieve the Sigil of Trollbane.",al={"sigil of trollbane questgiver","who gives sigil of trollbane","where do i start sigil of trollbane"}},{q="Where is Prince Galen Trollbane located?",a="Prince Galen Trollbane waits in a chapel far inside Stromgarde, in the districts held by the militia.",al={"prince galen trollbane location","where is galen trollbane","galen trollbane stromgarde"}},{q="Why is the Sigil of Trollbane needed?",a="The Sigil of Trollbane is the last sigil Zengu needs to open Thoras Trollbane's tomb. Thoras's son, Prince Galen, keeps it himself.",al={"purpose of sigil of trollbane","why get sigil of trollbane"}},{q="What comes after obtaining the Sigil of Trollbane?",a="After you obtain the Sigil of Trollbane, the chain continues with Trol'kalar.",al={"next quest after sigil of trollbane","what follows sigil of trollbane"}}},kw={"galen trollbane","hammerfall","sigil of arathor","stromgarde","trol'kalar","zengu","zul'gurub"},rel={"quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:638","subzone:zul-gurub","topic:troll"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Zengu",level="42",faction="Horde",id=644},src={"Sigil of Trollbane (quest)"}}
E["quest:645"] = {t="quest",n="Trol'kalar",z="arathi",s="At Stromgarde, Zengu sends you after Trol'kalar, now that four sigils have joined as one.",h="At Stromgarde, Zengu sends you after Trol'kalar, now that four sigils have joined as one.",sec={{t="One Sigil from Four",b="Zengu has seen the four sigils unite as the Sigil of Ignaeus. He believes their union can break the wardings on Trollbane's tomb. The tomb lies in the Sanctum behind Stromgarde's chapel, and Zengu sends you there to retrieve Trol'kalar. A fenced path to the right of the chapel entrance descends to the crypt.",sp=0},{t="The Tomb Opens",b="Etchings on Trollbane's tomb match the glowing lines of the sigil. When they meet, a flash of light swallows the sigil. Trol'kalar, the legendary sword, is freed from the stone hands that held it.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to retrieve Trol'kalar?",a="Zengu sends you to retrieve Trol'kalar after the four sigils unite as the Sigil of Ignaeus.",al={"who gives this quest","quest giver","zengu"}},{q="Where is Trollbane's tomb located?",a="Trollbane's remains lie in the Sanctum behind Stromgarde's chapel. A fenced path to the right of the chapel entrance descends to the crypt.",al={"where is the tomb","tomb location","crypt location"}},{q="What happens to the four sigils?",a="The four sigils unite as the Sigil of Ignaeus. Zengu believes it can break the wardings on Trollbane's tomb.",al={"what happened to sigils","sigil of ignaeus"}},{q="What is the previous step in this chain?",a="Sigil of Trollbane, the last of the four sigils, comes before this.",al={"previous quest","prior quest","sigil of trollbane"}}},kw={"crypt","sanctum","sigil of ignaeus","stromgarde","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu"},rel={"subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep","subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","quest:638"},m={start="Zengu",["end"]="Trollbane's Tomb",level="42",faction="Horde",id=645},src={"Trol'kalar (Classic)"}}
E["quest:646"] = {t="quest",n="Trol'kalar",z="arathi",s="At Trollbane's Tomb, Trol'kalar slips free of its stone sheath as the light fades. You carry the sword to Zengu in Hammerfall.",h="At Trollbane's Tomb, Trol'kalar slips free of its stone sheath as the light fades.",sec={{t="A Sword Set Free",b="At Trollbane's Tomb, you find Trol'kalar free of its stone sheath. You carry the sheathed sword to Zengu in Hammerfall, in the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="What Zengu Says",b="Zengu says Strom and Arathor's forces preyed on the trolls for generations. Now his people hold their greatest weapon, and the slow advance into Zul'Gurub's humid forests will no longer be a struggle. The Darkspear trolls are in your debt, he says. He will deliver the sword to Nimboya at Grom'gol.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Trol'kalar need to go?",a="Carry the sword, still in its stone sheath, to Zengu in Hammerfall, in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where do i take trolkalar","trol'kalar delivery","trolkalar hand in"}},{q="Where do I find the sword?",a="Find the sword at Trollbane's Tomb, where the fading light has freed it from its stone sheath.",al={"where is trol'kalar","trolkalar location"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="This follows the earlier Trol'kalar step and is the last step in the long chain.",al={"trol'kalar previous","trolkalar chain"}}},kw={"arathi","hammerfall","nimboya","trol'kalar","trollbane","zengu","zul'gurub"},rel={"quest:645","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:zul-gurub","topic:troll","zone:arathi"},m={start="Trollbane's Tomb",["end"]="Zengu",level="42",faction="Horde",id=646},src={"Trol'kalar (2)"}}
E["quest:651"] = {t="quest",n="Stones of Binding",z="arathi",s="In Arathi, four Stones of Binding hold Myzrael beneath the ground. A voice from the iridescent shards says the strongest stone needs keys from the other three.",h="In Arathi, four Stones of Binding hold Myzrael beneath the ground.",sec={{t="Four Stones",b="Across Arathi, four stones keep Myzrael beneath the ground, a voice says. The Stone of Inner Binding is strongest, and keys from the Stones of West, East and Outer Binding can unlock it. Gather the Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key. Guardians watch the stones, though someone clever or lucky may find a way to banish them. Carry the keys to the Stone of Inner Binding.",sp=0},{t="At the Inner Stone",b="Myzrael’s voice comes from the stone. The Stones of Binding are open, the shackles are loosening, and freedom draws closer. Myzrael hails you as a noble rescuer.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does this step come from?",a="This step follows The Princess Trapped. Its voice comes from the iridescent shards.",al={"stones of binding quest giver","who gives stones of binding","where to start stones of binding"}},{q="What are the four Stones of Binding?",a="The four are the Stone of West Binding, the Stone of East Binding, the Stone of Outer Binding and the strongest, the Stone of Inner Binding.",al={"which stones of binding","arathi binding stones","four stones"}},{q="Which keys are needed to unlock the inner stone?",a="The Burning Key, the Cresting Key and the Thundering Key are gathered from the Stones of West, East and Outer Binding.",al={"binding keys","what keys are needed","keys for stone of inner binding"}},{q="Who guards the binding stones?",a="Guardians watch over the stones, though a clever or lucky adventurer may find a way to banish them.",al={"stone guardians","who guards the stones","binding stone protectors"}},{q="Where must the keys be delivered?",a="Carry the keys to the mightiest stone, the Stone of Inner Binding. It must be unlocked before the others will open.",al={"where do i take the keys","turn in stones of binding","stone of inner binding location"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","burning key","cresting key","iridescent shards","myzrael","stone of inner binding","stones of binding","thundering key"},rel={"quest:642","quest:652","zone:arathi"},m={start="Iridescent Shards",["end"]="Stone of Inner Binding",level="38",id=651},src={"Classic quest text: Stones of Binding"}}
E["quest:652"] = {t="quest",n="Breaking the Keystone",z="arathi",s="The voice has more freedom now, though the Keystone still binds it. The Keystone lies among a ring of stones, and Fozruk holds the key the watchers call the Rod of Order.",h="The voice has more freedom now, though the Keystone still binds it.",sec={{t="The Last Lock",b="Opening the Stones of Binding eased the voice's confinement, but one lock still holds the Keystone. It lies among the circle of stones around you. Fozruk, a stone watcher and one of its captors, holds the key the watchers call the Rod of Order. Carry the rod to the Keystone and open the lock. The voice promises gratitude that will shake the earth to its roots. Geomantic energy fills the Keystone.",sp=0},{t="At the Keystone",b="When you set the rod into the Keystone, a tremor runs beneath you.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What comes before this step?",a="The Stones of Binding came first. Opening them eased much of the voice's confinement.",al={"prerequisite","previous quest","stones of binding prerequisite"}},{q="Who is Fozruk?",a="Fozruk is a stone watcher and one of the voice's captors. He holds the key to the Keystone.",al={"who is fozruk","fozruk lore","stone watcher fozruk"}},{q="What is the Rod of Order?",a="The stone watchers call the key to the Keystone the Rod of Order. Fozruk holds it.",al={"rod of order","what is rod of order","keystone key"}},{q="Where is the Keystone?",a="The Keystone lies among a circle of stones in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where is breaking the keystone","keystone location","stone circle arathi"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","fozruk","keystone","rod of order","stone of inner binding","stone watcher"},rel={"quest:651","zone:arathi"},m={start="Stone of Inner Binding",["end"]="Keystone",level="42",id=652},src={"Classic quest text: Breaking the Keystone"}}
E["quest:653"] = {t="quest",n="Myzrael's Allies",z="arathi",s="Myzrael is free, yet she must gather strength before she can face her captors. She calls you a noble ally and sends you to Gerrig Bonegrip in a shop in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, where he knows how to summon her.",h="Myzrael is free, yet she must gather strength before she can face her captors.",sec={{t="Free to Gather Strength",b="Myzrael is free, but not strong enough to face her captors. They would overpower her now and lock her away again. So she will gather strength in hiding. When she is ready, she means to face the giants and make them rue the day they held her. She calls you a noble ally and says she will need your help to summon her to the surface.",sp=0},{t="Word for Gerrig Bonegrip",b="Myzrael sends you to Gerrig Bonegrip, whose shop is in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern. He knows how to summon her.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Gerrig Bonegrip be found?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip keeps a shop in Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern.",al={"gerrig bonegrip location","where is gerrig bonegrip","find gerrig bonegrip"}},{q="Why is Myzrael remaining in hiding?",a="Myzrael must gather strength first. If her captors faced her now, they would overpower her and imprison her again.",al={"why is myzrael hiding","where is myzrael going"}},{q="Who are the captors Myzrael speaks of?",a="Myzrael means the giants who had wardship of her. She says she will confront them in time and make them rue having held her.",al={"myzrael captors","who imprisoned myzrael","myzrael giants"}},{q="Why does Myzrael send you to Ironforge?",a="Myzrael sends you to Gerrig Bonegrip because he knows how she can be summoned. She will need your help to summon her to the surface when she is ready.",al={"why go to ironforge","purpose of visiting gerrig"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","giants","ironforge","keystone","myzrael"},rel={"npc:gerrig-bonegrip","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ironforge","zone:arathi"},m={start="Keystone",["end"]="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="40",faction="Alliance",id=653},src={"Myzrael's Allies (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:656"] = {t="quest",n="Summoning the Princess",z="arathi",s="At the Shards of Myzrael, you summon Myzrael and face her before she grows strong enough to challenge her captors. Theldurin the Lost wants her defeated and her Eldritch Shackles bound to the Shards.",h="At the Shards of Myzrael, you summon Myzrael and face her before she grows strong enough to challenge her...",sec={{t="Why She Must Be Stopped",b="Theldurin fears Myzrael will grow strong enough to turn against her captors. Some say she can be controlled. But Theldurin asks why the giants would have chained her if that were true.",sp=0},{t="At the Shards",b="You take the Scroll of Myzrael to the Shards, where you first spoke with her, and call her forth. Once Myzrael is defeated, you bind her Eldritch Shackles to the Shards and trap her again.",sp=0},{t="When the Shackles Are Placed",b="As Myzrael's shackles settle around the Shards, a wail rises from far below, then a roar. The Shards no longer offer warmth or safety. They pulse with menace, as though the thing beneath them bears ill will toward the surface.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to fight Myzrael?",a="Theldurin the Lost sends you to defeat Myzrael before her strength grows enough to challenge her captors.",al={"quest giver","who gives summoning the princess","theldurin quest"}},{q="Where does the summoning take place?",a="You summon Myzrael at the Shards of Myzrael, where you first spoke with her.",al={"where to summon myzrael","shards of myzrael location","summoning spot"}},{q="Why does Theldurin want Myzrael defeated?",a="Theldurin fears Myzrael will grow strong enough to challenge her captors. He asks why the giants chained her if she could truly be controlled.",al={"why kill myzrael","theldurin motivation","why summon her"}},{q="How is Myzrael summoned?",a="You summon Myzrael at the Shards of Myzrael with the Scroll of Myzrael.",al={"how to summon her","scroll of myzrael use","summoning process"}},{q="What do you do with the Eldritch Shackles?",a="After defeating Myzrael, you bind her Eldritch Shackles to the Shards and trap her again.",al={"what item do i need","eldritch shackles","shackles of myzrael"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","eldritch shackles","myzrael","scroll of myzrael","shards of myzrael","theldurin the lost"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","zone:arathi"},m={start="Theldurin the Lost",["end"]="Shards of Myzrael",level="50",id=656},src={"Summoning the Princess"}}
E["quest:662"] = {t="quest",n="Deep Sea Salvage",z="arathi",s="After Land Ho!, First Mate Nilzlix asks you to recover the charts and logs from two wrecks before anyone leaves the cove.",h="After Land Ho!, First Mate Nilzlix asks you to recover the charts and logs from two wrecks before anyone...",sec={{t="Two Ships Lost in the Reef",b="O'Breen brought three ships into the cove, certain treasure lay there. The Harbinger docked safely. But the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine reached the reef as the tides began to fall. Both struck a temple-like structure and sank fast.",sp=0},{t="What Nilzlix Wants Back",b="First Mate Nilzlix wants you to recover the logs and charts from both wrecks. He fears the information could reach prying eyes. If enemies found it, Fleet Master Seahorn would force the crew down the plank.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine sink?",a="The Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine entered the cove as the tides began to fall. Both struck a temple-like structure in the reef and sank quickly.",al={"why did the ships wreck","how did the ships sink","arathi cove shipwreck cause"}},{q="Who is First Mate Nilzlix?",a="First Mate Nilzlix speaks of the three ships O'Breen led into the cove. He wants you to recover the logs and charts from the two sunken ships.",al={"nilzlix","who gives deep sea salvage"}},{q="Why are the charts and logs so important?",a="Nilzlix fears prying eyes will find the information left behind. If enemies got hold of it, he says Fleet Master Seahorn would force the crew down the plank.",al={"why recover logs","why charts and logs"}},{q="What ship made it to safety?",a="Only the Harbinger docked safely in the cove. The other two ships sank.",al={"which ship survived","harbinger ship"}},{q="Who is Fleet Master Seahorn?",a="Nilzlix names Fleet Master Seahorn as the one who would force the crew down the plank if enemy hands got the records.",al={"fleet master seahorn role","who is seahorn"}},{q="What came before this task?",a="Land Ho! came before this.",al={"deep sea salvage prerequisite","previous quest"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","booty bay","deep sea salvage","harbinger","maiden's folly","nilzlix","o'breen","seahorn","spirit of silverpine"},rel={"quest:663","npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="First Mate Nilzlix",["end"]="First Mate Nilzlix",level="40",id=662},src={"Deep Sea Salvage"}}
E["quest:663"] = {t="quest",n="Land Ho!",z="arathi",s="At Faldir's Cove, Lolo warns you that Captain O'Breen's brief stop may last far longer than planned. The Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly are lost, and Lolo directs you to the captain.",h="At Faldir's Cove, Lolo warns you that Captain O'Breen's brief stop may last far longer than planned.",sec={{t="Lolo's Welcome",b="Lolo greets you at Faldir's Cove and tells you what has gone wrong. Captain O'Breen promised the crew only a few hours ashore to gather treasure before sailing back to Booty Bay. Lolo doubts they will be away so briefly.\n\nThe Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly, two ships in the formation, now lie on the sea floor. If you mean to stay, Lolo says to speak with the captain.",sp=0},{t="The Captain's Account",b="Captain O'Breen fears Seahorn will take the ship if word of the disaster spreads. A contraption belonging to the Professor pointed toward lost treasure near Faldir's Cove. So the Harbinger docked there and signaled the other two ships to follow.\n\nThen the sea rumbled and the water drew back. Both ships struck the reef. O'Breen says it is no ordinary reef, and something lies below. He promises handsome payment to anyone who helps the crew.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the other ships?",a="The Spirit of Silverpine and the Maiden's Folly were lost and now lie on the sea floor.",al={"where are the other ships","sunken ships faldir","what sank the ships"}},{q="Why did the crew come to Faldir's Cove?",a="Captain O'Breen brought the crew to Faldir's Cove to gather treasure. They expected to stay only a few hours before sailing back to Booty Bay.",al={"why are they here","purpose of expedition","what brought them to arathi"}},{q="Who should you talk to at Faldir's Cove?",a="Lolo the lookout suggests you speak with Captain O'Breen at Faldir's Cove if you plan to stay.",al={"who is captain o'breen","where is shakes o'breen"}}},kw={"booty bay","faldir's cove","harbinger","lolo the lookout","maiden's folly","seahorn","shakes o'breen","spirit of silverpine"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","quest:662","quest:665","quest:664","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Lolo the Lookout",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="35",id=663},src={"Land Ho!"}}
E["quest:664"] = {t="quest",n="Drowned Sorrows",z="arathi",s="At Faldir's Cove, Captain Steelgut mourns the Maiden's Folly and asks you to kill the Daggerspine naga who slew the wreck's survivors.",h="At Faldir's Cove, Captain Steelgut mourns the Maiden's Folly and asks you to kill the Daggerspine naga who...",sec={{t="A Captain by the Fire",b="At Faldir's Cove, Captain Steelgut sits by the fire and wishes the sea had taken him too. His crew fought hard to save the Maiden's Folly, but water rushed in all at once and the ship sank. O'Breen reached shore safely, while the naga killed the other survivors. Steelgut wants ten Daggerspine raiders and three Daggerspine sorceresses dead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Steelgut?",a="Captain Steelgut commanded the Maiden's Folly. After the ship was lost, he sat by a fire at Faldir's Cove.",al={"captain steelgut","steelgut","who is the quest giver"}},{q="What happened to the Maiden's Folly?",a="Steelgut says the sea sank the Maiden's Folly. The ship was afloat, then water rushed in all at once despite the crew's hard fight to save it.",al={"maidens folly","what happened to the ship","why did steelgut crash"}},{q="Why does Captain Steelgut want the naga killed?",a="The naga killed the wreck's survivors, and Steelgut wants them dead.",al={"why kill naga","steelgut revenge","daggerspine reason"}},{q="Which naga does Steelgut want dead?",a="Ten Daggerspine raiders and three Daggerspine sorceresses, as Steelgut asks.",al={"which naga to kill","target naga","daggerspine targets"}}},kw={"arathi","daggerspine","faldir's cove","maiden's folly","naga","o'breen","raider","sorceress","steelgut"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","topic:naga","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Steelgut",["end"]="Captain Steelgut",level="40",id=664},src={"Drowned Sorrows (Classic)"}}
E["quest:665"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Professor Phizzlethorpe and Doctor Draxlegauge now aid the Blackwater Raiders in their search for lost elven treasure. Before the search can begin, the professor needs your protection while he charges goggles for the dark sea.",h="Professor Phizzlethorpe and Doctor Draxlegauge now aid the Blackwater Raiders in their search for lost elven...",sec={{t="Charging the Goggles",b="Professor Phizzlethorpe asks you to guard him as he prepares for a search beneath the dark sea. Doctor Draxlegauge built goggles to find the lost gems, but they need power from an enchanted stone in a cave a short way uphill. The cave is cursed, and those who draw near are ambushed. Defend the professor while he draws the stone’s energy into the goggles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is asking for help?",a="Professor Phizzlethorpe asks you to guard him on the way to and from the cave while he charges Doctor Draxlegauge’s goggles at the enchanted stone.",al={"who gives this quest","phizzlethorpe","quest giver"}},{q="Why do the goggles need to be charged?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge built the goggles to find the lost gems in the dark sea. They need the stone’s power before they can work.",al={"why charge goggles","goggles purpose","what are the goggles for"}},{q="Why does the professor need an escort?",a="The cave is cursed, and those who draw near are ambushed. You need to defend Professor Phizzlethorpe while he channels the stone’s energy.",al={"why protect phizzlethorpe","what is in the cave"}},{q="Who are the professor and the doctor working for?",a="Professor Phizzlethorpe says he and Doctor Draxlegauge are now full-fledged Blackwater Raiders. Their duty is to help Mr. O’Breen find the lost elven treasure.",al={"who are they helping","mr obreen","blackwater raiders"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","draxlegauge","enchanted stone","goggles","o'breen","phizzlethorpe","sunken treasure"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:gnome"},m={start="Professor Phizzlethorpe",["end"]="Doctor Draxlegauge",level="40",id=665},src={"Sunken Treasure (1)"}}
E["quest:666"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="In Faldir's Cove, Doctor Draxlegauge lends you his goggles to find ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen. He expects them back when you finish.",h="In Faldir's Cove, Doctor Draxlegauge lends you his goggles to find ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen.",sec={{t="Gems Turned to Stone",b="The elven gems have lain on the sea floor so long that thick stone has hardened around them. The Goggles of Gem Hunting hold the power to find them through those stony shells. Proud of the gnomish ingenuity behind the goggles, Doctor Draxlegauge lends them to you. The gems are for Captain O'Breen.",sp=0},{t="Dry Land for the Doctor",b="Doctor Draxlegauge says scientific work keeps him on safe, dry land, though he could swim down himself. He expects you to return the goggles afterward. Captain O'Breen, he says, will have plenty of use for them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to gather the gems?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge, waiting in Faldir's Cove, sends you to gather ten elven gems for Captain O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 2","quest giver sunken treasure"}},{q="Why are special goggles required for the search?",a="Years on the sea floor have hardened the gems into thick stone. The power in the Goggles of Gem Hunting lets you find them easily.",al={"why goggles of gem hunting","what do the goggles do"}},{q="Why doesn't Doctor Draxlegauge dive for the gems himself?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge says important scientific work keeps him on safe, dry land.",al={"why doesn't draxlegauge swim","why draxlegauge stays on land"}},{q="Can you keep the Goggles of Gem Hunting?",a="No. Doctor Draxlegauge lends you the goggles and expects them back when you finish. Captain O'Breen will use them often.",al={"keep gem hunting goggles","do i return goggles"}},{q="Where does this fall in the Sunken Treasure chain?",a="This follows the first part of Sunken Treasure, when Professor Phizzlethorpe charged the goggles. A third part follows.",al={"what comes before this","what is the next step"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","captain o'breen","doctor draxlegauge","elven gem","faldir's cove","fleet master seahorn","goggles of gem hunting","sunken treasure"},rel={"subzone:faldir-s-cove","zone:arathi","npc:fleet-master-seahorn"},m={start="Doctor Draxlegauge",["end"]="Doctor Draxlegauge",level="40",id=666},src={"Sunken Treasure (2)"}}
E["quest:667"] = {t="quest",n="Death From Below",z="arathi",s="Aboard Shakes O'Breen's ship in the Arathi Highlands, the Daggerspine naga gather to strike. You stand with O'Breen, man the cannon, and help the crew sail back to Booty Bay.",h="Aboard Shakes O'Breen's ship in the Arathi Highlands, the Daggerspine naga gather to strike.",sec={{t="Holding the Deck",b="After the Sunken Treasure, Shakes O'Breen sees the Daggerspine naga gathering to attack. They are ruthless and will keep coming until O'Breen is dead. O'Breen puts the crew's safety ahead of their own and asks you to defend them. Without O'Breen's knowledge of the seas, the crew cannot reach Booty Bay. So you wait aboard with O'Breen for the naga to rise from the water.",sp=0},{t="Afterward",b="When the attack ends, O'Breen says the ship will leave as soon as the tide rises. O'Breen would have offered you a place on the crew, but sees that you have bigger fish to fry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is attacking Shakes O'Breen?",a="The Daggerspine naga gather to attack Shakes O'Breen. They come from the sea and will keep coming until O'Breen is dead.",al={"who attacks shakes","who are the attackers","daggerspine attack"}},{q="Why is protecting Shakes O'Breen so vital to the crew?",a="Shakes O'Breen puts the crew's safety ahead of their own. Without O'Breen's knowledge of the seas, the crew cannot sail back to Booty Bay.",al={"why protect shakes obreen","why is shakes important","shakes obreen navigation"}},{q="How do you repel the naga assault?",a="You stay aboard Shakes O'Breen's ship and man the cannon. You drive back the naga as they come from the sea.",al={"how to beat death from below","how to defend shakes","cannon defense"}},{q="Where does this defense take place?",a="You defend Shakes O'Breen's ship in the Arathi Highlands as the naga come from the sea.",al={"where is death from below","death from below location"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","booty bay","daggerspine","naga","shakes o'breen","ship cannon"},rel={"topic:naga","zone:arathi","subzone:booty-bay"},m={start="Shakes O'Breen",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="44",id=667},src={"Death From Below (Classic)"}}
E["quest:668"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Doctor Draxlegauge sends you to Captain O'Breen, who waits at the bridge for the elven gems. After weeks among pirates, the doctor and the professor have learned that keeping pirate treasure is bad for their health.",h="Doctor Draxlegauge sends you to Captain O'Breen, who waits at the bridge for the elven gems.",sec={{t="Treasure for the Captain",b="Doctor Draxlegauge is eager to bring Captain O'Breen the elven gems. The captain waits at the bridge and wants to see them for himself. After weeks among these pirates, the doctor and the professor have learned that keeping pirate treasure is bad for their health. So Draxlegauge gives you the gems to carry to O'Breen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Captain O'Breen?",a="Doctor Draxlegauge gives you the elven gems to carry to Captain O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 3","draxlegauge quest"}},{q="Why is Doctor Draxlegauge so eager to give up the gems?",a="After weeks among these pirates, Doctor Draxlegauge and the professor have learned that keeping pirate treasure is bad for their health.",al={"why hand over elven gems","why give gems to pirate"}},{q="Where does this fall in the chain?",a="This follows the second part of Sunken Treasure, and a fourth part comes after it.",al={"sunken treasure chain position","what comes before sunken treasure 3"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","captain o'breen","doctor draxlegauge","elven gems","pirates","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:pirate","topic:gnome"},m={start="Doctor Draxlegauge",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="40",id=668},src={"Sunken Treasure (3)"}}
E["quest:669"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="In Sunken Treasure, Shakes O'Breen is held back by the low tide and watchful creatures, so word must reach Booty Bay.",h="In Sunken Treasure, Shakes O'Breen is held back by the low tide and watchful creatures, so word must reach...",sec={{t="Word for Booty Bay",b="Shakes O'Breen needs Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay to hear of the find at once. The tide is too low for him to leave, and the creatures his crew disturbed watch every move. He asks you to tell Seahorn the treasure has been found and more is being brought up. You carry a sample elven gem as proof.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why can't Shakes O'Breen deliver the gem himself?",a="The tide is too low for Shakes O'Breen and his crew to leave, and the creatures they disturbed watch their movements.",al={"why cant shakes leave","why is shakes stuck","why does shakes need a courier"}},{q="Who is Fleet Master Seahorn?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn is in Booty Bay, and O'Breen wants him to hear of the find at once.",al={"who is seahorn","where is fleet master seahorn"}},{q="What proof is being carried to Booty Bay?",a="You carry a sample elven gem to prove the treasure was found and more is being brought up.",al={"what is the proof","what gem is delivered"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","booty bay","fleet master seahorn","sample elven gem","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Shakes O'Breen",["end"]="Fleet Master Seahorn",level="40",id=669},src={"Sunken Treasure (4)"}}
E["quest:670"] = {t="quest",n="Sunken Treasure",z="arathi",s="Fleet Master Seahorn waits in Booty Bay with a letter for Shakes O'Breen off the Arathi coast. His ships cannot sail until they restock.",h="Fleet Master Seahorn waits in Booty Bay with a letter for Shakes O'Breen off the Arathi coast.",sec={{t="A Letter for O'Breen",b="Fleet Master Seahorn sees an adventurer in you. His ships must restock before they can leave Booty Bay. Heavy things are brewing here and abroad, he says, and he has a secret letter for Shakes O'Breen off the Arathi coast. Can he trust you to deliver it safely and keep it confidential?",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to deliver this letter?",a="Fleet Master Seahorn in Booty Bay gives you a sealed letter for Shakes O'Breen.",al={"who gives sunken treasure 5","who starts this quest","seahorns letter questgiver"}},{q="Why doesn't Fleet Master Seahorn deliver the letter himself?",a="His ships cannot sail from Booty Bay until they restock.",al={"why can't seahorn leave booty bay","why is fleet master seahorn stuck"}},{q="Where is Shakes O'Breen located?",a="Shakes O'Breen is busy off the coast of the Arathi Highlands.",al={"where to find shakes obreen","shakes obreen location","where is shakes"}},{q="What came before this delivery?",a="This delivery follows the fourth part of Sunken Treasure.",al={"sunken treasure chain","what quest comes before sunken treasure 5"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","blackwater raiders","booty bay","fleet master seahorn","seahorn's sealed letter","shakes o'breen","sunken treasure"},rel={"npc:fleet-master-seahorn","subzone:booty-bay","zone:arathi"},m={start="Fleet Master Seahorn",["end"]="Shakes O'Breen",level="40",id=670},src={"Sunken Treasure (5)"}}
E["quest:673"] = {t="quest",n="Foul Magics",z="arathi",s="In Hammerfall, Tor'gan fears a warlock in Stromgarde is calling demons with an arcane relic. Your first work for him has led to a hunt for the warlock and the relic.",h="In Hammerfall, Tor'gan fears a warlock in Stromgarde is calling demons with an arcane relic.",sec={{t="A Warlock in Stromgarde",b="Tor'gan is certain a warlock within Stromgarde's walls uses an arcane relic to call up terrible demons in great numbers. The burning in his blood grows by the day. So he sends you to find and kill the warlock, then bring back the magical object on the warlock's body. He means to destroy it before its power can taint the land. The warlock is Marez Cowl, and the object is a Befouled Bloodstone Orb.",sp=0},{t="What the Orb Recalls",b="With the orb destroyed, Tor'gan expects his restless nights to give way to peaceful sleep. The orb recalls the dreadful hold demons once had over the orcs. That hold endured until Hellscream freed them from their curse.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to hunt the warlock?",a="Tor'gan in Hammerfall sends you into Stromgarde to find the warlock and bring him the magical object on the warlock's body.",al={"who gives foul magics","foul magics quest giver","torgan quest"}},{q="Where is the warlock located?",a="Marez Cowl hides within Stromgarde's walls, west of and outside the Keep, behind a building. You can hear her channeling a spell.",al={"where is marez cowl","stromgarde warlock location","where to find marez cowl"}},{q="What relic are you sent to retrieve?",a="You are sent to retrieve Marez Cowl's Befouled Bloodstone Orb. Tor'gan wants it brought to him for destruction.",al={"what item does torgan want","befouled bloodstone orb","foul magics item"}},{q="Why does Tor'gan want the warlock stopped?",a="The warlock has summoned terrible demons in large numbers using an arcane relic. Tor'gan wants you to remove the relic's power and destroy the orb before it can taint the land.",al={"why destroy the orb","torgan motivation","why stop the warlock"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","hammerfall","marez cowl","stromgarde","torgan","warlock"},rel={"quest:671","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:stromgarde-keep","topic:warlock","zone:arathi"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="40",faction="Horde",id=673},src={"Foul Magics (2)"}}
E["quest:679"] = {t="quest",n="Call to Arms",z="arathi",s="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel sends you after the Boulderfist leaders in Stromgarde. After your earlier work, he says it is time to strike the head from the beast.",h="At Hammerfall, Drum Fel sends you after the Boulderfist leaders in Stromgarde.",sec={{t="The Head of the Beast",b="Drum Fel says you are ready to help deliver one last great blow. The Boulderfist leaders have made their lair in Stromgarde’s ruins, which he calls a symbol of human frailty. He sends you to hunt down the lords and the shaman who serve them. They lead attacks meant to drive the Horde from these lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to fight the Boulderfist leaders?",a="Drum Fel sends you from Hammerfall, the Horde outpost in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who gives call to arms","drum fel quest","who starts call to arms 3"}},{q="Where are the Boulderfist lords and shaman located?",a="The Boulderfist lords and shaman leading the attacks are holed up in Stromgarde’s ruins, Drum Fel says.",al={"where are boulderfist lords","boulderfist shaman location","where to find ogre leaders"}},{q="Where does this step fit into the chain?",a="This follows the previous Call to Arms and is the last step in the chain that begins with Tallow in Tarren Mill.",al={"what came before call to arms 3","call to arms chain","hammerfall ogre chain"}},{q="What does Drum Fel want done to the Boulderfist leaders?",a="Drum Fel wants you to kill the lords and shaman leading the attacks in one last great blow. They mean to drive the Horde from these lands.",al={"why kill boulderfist lords","why attack stromgarde ogres"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist lords","boulderfist shaman","drum fel","hammerfall","stromgarde"},rel={"quest:677","subzone:hammerfall","npc:drum-fel","quest:680","quest:676","npc:tallow","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:arathi"},m={start="Drum Fel",["end"]="Drum Fel",level="40",faction="Horde",id=679},src={"Call to Arms (3)"}}
E["quest:680"] = {t="quest",n="The Real Threat",z="arathi",s="Korin Fel asks you to end the attacks on Hammerfall by slaying Or'Kalar and bringing her his head.",h="Korin Fel asks you to end the attacks on Hammerfall by slaying Or'Kalar and bringing her his head.",sec={{t="A Grudge Against Her Husband",b="Korin Fel says you serve her husband well, though he does not know why Hammerfall is under attack. Or'Kalar serves Mug'thol in Stromgarde and seeks her husband's death. Years ago, her husband defeated the ogre. Now Korin's auguries warn that Or'Kalar has set a trap for him.",sp=0},{t="What Korin Hides",b="Korin has hidden the signs of Or'Kalar's presence from her husband. She fears he would rush off foolishly if he knew where the ogre was, so she asks you to help instead. Or'Kalar is near the Tower of Arathor. Korin expects his death to end the attacks on Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Korin Fel trying to protect?",a="Korin Fel is trying to protect her husband. Her auguries warn that Or'Kalar has set a trap for him. The ogre wants him dead because he defeated him years ago.",al={"korin husband","why does korin need help"}},{q="Why is Or'Kalar attacking Hammerfall?",a="Or'Kalar attacks Hammerfall as Mug'thol's pawn in Stromgarde. He hates Korin Fel's husband, who defeated him years ago. Korin says Or'Kalar's death would stop the attacks.",al={"why does or'kalar hate korin's husband","who is or'kalar","or'kalar motive"}},{q="Where is Or'Kalar located?",a="Close to the Tower of Arathor.",al={"or'kalar location","where to find or'kalar","find or'kalar"}},{q="Why does Korin keep the threat a secret from her husband?",a="Korin fears her husband would rush off foolishly if he learned where Or'Kalar was. So she has hidden every sign of the ogre's presence.",al={"why keep it secret","why hide or'kalar","korin secret"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","hammerfall","korin fel","mug'thol","or'kalar","stromgarde","tower of arathor"},rel={"quest:677","quest:676","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:tower-of-arathor","zone:arathi"},m={start="Korin Fel",["end"]="Korin Fel",level="40",faction="Horde",id=680},src={"The Real Threat (Classic)"}}
E["quest:681"] = {t="quest",n="Northfold Manor",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials seeks your help against the Syndicate at Northfold Manor. Their hold between Stromgarde's defenders and Southshore slows supplies.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials seeks your help against the Syndicate at Northfold Manor.",sec={{t="A Struggling Defense",b="Ogres, the Syndicate and the Alliance divide Stromgarde, and the factions fight to a bloody stalemate. The Alliance's forces dwindle as their enemies grow. The defenders need help from Southshore, but supplies arrive slowly.",sp=0},{t="The Syndicate at the Manor",b="The Syndicate holds the ground between the defenders and Southshore. Captain Nials asks you to go to Northfold Manor, the Syndicate's base, and cut down their highwaymen and mercenaries. He hopes easing their pressure will let more supply trains through.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Captain Nials want the Syndicate attacked at Northfold Manor?",a="The Syndicate holds the land between the defenders and Southshore. Captain Nials hopes that slaying them at their base will ease the pressure on the supply trains.",al={"why attack northfold manor","nials objective","purpose of northfold manor quest"}},{q="What is the current situation in Stromgarde?",a="Ogres, the Syndicate and the Alliance have divided Stromgarde, and the factions fight to a bloody stalemate. The Alliance's forces dwindle while its enemies grow.",al={"stromgarde war status","who controls stromgarde","state of stromgarde"}},{q="Where are the Alliance supplies coming from?",a="The defenders look to Southshore for help, but the Syndicate's hold on the land between makes supplies difficult to receive.",al={"who supplies refuge pointe","southshore supplies","where do shipments originate"}},{q="Which enemies need to be eliminated at the manor?",a="Ten Syndicate Highwaymen and six Syndicate Mercenaries at Northfold Manor.",al={"who to kill at northfold","northfold targets","syndicate enemies list"}}},kw={"captain nials","highwayman","mercenary","northfold manor","refuge pointe","southshore","stromgarde","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:northfold-manor","topic:syndicate","subzone:southshore","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Nials",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="31",faction="Alliance",id=681},src={"Northfold Manor (Classic)"}}
E["quest:682"] = {t="quest",n="Stromgarde Badges",z="arathi",s="In Stromgarde, the Syndicate pays for militia badges taken from the fallen. At Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials wants them brought back.",h="In Stromgarde, the Syndicate pays for militia badges taken from the fallen.",sec={{t="A Bounty on Soldiers",b="The Syndicate fights a contingent of militia in Stromgarde. Its leaders offer gold for every badge taken from a slain militiaman, hoping to turn their followers against the better-trained soldiers. Captain Nials calls the Syndicate cutthroats and refuses to let them keep trophies from the brave fallen. You enter the part of Stromgarde they hold and bring the badges back to Refuge Pointe. Nials wants them to learn they cannot profit from the dead.",sp=0},{t="After the Hunt",b="Captain Nials promises to tell the fallen militiamen's relatives that their kin died in battle. The news is grim, but he believes it is better than leaving a family to wonder what became of someone who went missing.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does the Syndicate want Stromgarde badges?",a="Syndicate leaders offer gold for every badge taken from a fallen militiaman. They hope the payment will drive their followers to fight the better-trained troops.",al={"why syndicate badges","syndicate bounty stromgarde","why collect badges"}},{q="Where are the badges found?",a="You find the badges in the part of Stromgarde controlled by the Syndicate.",al={"where to find badges","stromgarde badge location","badge drop location"}},{q="Who orders the retrieval of the badges?",a="Captain Nials at Refuge Pointe orders the badges recovered. He will not let the Syndicate keep trophies from the fallen militia.",al={"who gives stromgarde badges","captain nials badge quest","questgiver stromgarde badges"}}},kw={"arathi","badges","captain nials","militia","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","topic:syndicate","zone:arathi"},m={start="Captain Nials",["end"]="Captain Nials",level="37",id=682},src={"Classic quest text: Stromgarde Badges"}}
E["quest:687"] = {t="quest",n="Theldurin the Lost",z="arathi",s="In the Badlands, the Twilight's Hammer hunts for Theldurin the Lost and the scroll of Myzrael he took when he fled.",h="In the Badlands, the Twilight's Hammer hunts for Theldurin the Lost and the scroll of Myzrael he took when he...",sec={{t="The Man Who Stole the Scroll",b="Theldurin once followed the Twilight's Hammer. Then his mind slipped, and he turned from its teachings. He fled with the scroll of Myzrael, and the order could not catch him.",sp=0},{t="Rumors of the Badlands",b="Word has reached the Twilight's Hammer that Theldurin hides in the Badlands, raving and mad. The order needs the scroll for the Lady's return. First, you must find the man who took it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Theldurin the Lost?",a="Theldurin the Lost once followed the Twilight's Hammer. After his mind slipped, he rejected its teachings and fled with the scroll of Myzrael.",al={"theldurin backstory","who is theldurin","theldurin lore"}},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer looking for him?",a="The Twilight's Hammer seeks Theldurin because he fled with the scroll of Myzrael. The order says it needs the scroll to bring the Lady back.",al={"why find theldurin","why do cultists want theldurin"}},{q="Where did Theldurin flee after leaving the order?",a="Rumors place Theldurin in the Badlands, though the Twilight's Hammer is not certain where he is.",al={"where is theldurin","theldurin location lore"}},{q="What comes directly before this search?",a="The search follows Myzrael's Allies.",al={"previous quest theldurin","prereq for theldurin the lost"}}},kw={"badlands","gerrig bonegrip","myzrael","scroll of myzrael","theldurin","theldurin the lost","twilight's hammer","zaruk"},rel={"npc:theldurin-the-lost","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:badlands","zone:arathi"},m={start="Gerrig Bonegrip, Zaruk",["end"]="Theldurin the Lost",level="40",faction="Both",id=687},src={"Theldurin the Lost (quest)"}}
E["quest:688"] = {t="quest",n="Myzrael's Allies",z="arathi",s="Through the keystone, Myzrael declares herself free, though still hidden from her captors. She sends you to Zaruk in Hammerfall, who knows how to summon her.",h="Through the keystone, Myzrael declares herself free, though still hidden from her captors.",sec={{t="Free but Hidden",b="Myzrael declares that she is free through the keystone. She must gather her strength out of sight. Her captors would overpower and imprison her again if they faced her now. In time, she vows to confront the giants who held her and make them regret keeping her.",sp=0},{t="Zaruk of Hammerfall",b="Myzrael calls you a noble ally and says she will need your aid again in time. When ready, she will have you summon her to the surface. For now, she sends you to Zaruk in Hammerfall, who knows how it can be done.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you to Zaruk?",a="Myzrael herself speaks through the keystone and tells you to see Zaruk in Hammerfall.",al={"who gives myzraels allies","quest giver myzraels allies","who speaks through the keystone"}},{q="Why is Myzrael hiding?",a="Myzrael says her captors would overpower and imprison her again if they faced her now. She hides while gathering strength.",al={"why doesnt myzrael fight","why is myzrael weak","why does myzrael hide"}},{q="Where can Zaruk be found?",a="Zaruk can be found in Hammerfall.",al={"zaruk location","where is zaruk","find zaruk"}},{q="What role does Zaruk play for Myzrael?",a="Myzrael says Zaruk knows how she can be summoned.",al={"why talk to zaruk","what does zaruk know","zaruk purpose"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","giants","hammerfall","keystone","myzrael","zaruk"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi"},m={start="Keystone",["end"]="Zaruk",level="40",faction="Horde",id=688},src={"Myzrael's Allies (Horde)"}}
E["quest:691"] = {t="quest",n="Worth Its Weight in Gold",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Apprentice Kryten needs reagents for Archmage Malin. He asks you to gather tusks, medicine pouches and a shadow hunter's knife from the Witherbark trolls of southeastern Arathi.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Apprentice Kryten needs reagents for Archmage Malin.",sec={{t="Malin's Reagents",b="Archmage Malin sent Kryten and Skuerto to Arathi for reagents. Kryten was unsure how to gather them until you arrived. He needs ten Witherbark tusks, four medicine pouches and one shadow hunter knife. The Witherbark trolls live in southeastern Arathi.",sp=0},{t="What the Witherbark Carry",b="Kryten's research says every Witherbark troll should have tusks. The witch doctors carry medicine pouches. The knife belongs to the mightiest shadow hunters, who receive it after completing their rites of passage. Only battle will show which one carries it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apprentice Kryten working for?",a="Archmage Malin sent Kryten and Skuerto to Arathi to gather reagents for him.",al={"who sent kryten","kryten master","why is kryten in arathi"}},{q="Where are the Witherbark trolls located?",a="In the southeast of Arathi, where the Witherbark make their home.",al={"witherbark location","where to find witherbark","witherbark village location"}},{q="Which trolls carry the medicine pouches?",a="Kryten's research says the Witherbark witch doctors carry medicine pouches. Any Witherbark troll should have tusks.",al={"medicine pouch source","who has medicine pouches","witherbark medicine pouch"}},{q="How do you find the shadow hunter knife?",a="The mightiest Witherbark shadow hunters carry the knife, given to them after their rites of passage. Only battle will reveal which one has it.",al={"shadow hunter knife location","who drops shadow hunter knife","rite of passage knife"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","arathi highlands","archmage malin","medicine pouch","refuge pointe","shadow hunter knife","skuerto","witherbark","witherbark tusk"},rel={"npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:witherbark-village","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},m={start="Apprentice Kryten",["end"]="Apprentice Kryten",level="36",faction="Alliance",id=691},src={"Worth Its Weight in Gold (Classic)"}}
E["quest:693"] = {t="quest",n="Wand over Fist",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto has found where Trelane's first item went. Kor'gresh holds Trelane's Wand of Invocation in Boulderfist Hall, and Skuerto wants it back.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto has found where Trelane's first item went.",sec={{t="The Ogre and the Wand",b="After your work for Apprentice Kryten, Skuerto has traced Trelane's first item to Kor'gresh. The ogre holds the wand in Boulderfist Hall and uses blasts of ice to keep his kin in line. Skuerto fears Kor'gresh is close to discovering all its powers. Boulderfist Hall lies south of Refuge Pointe, then east of Thandol Span.",sp=0},{t="Skuerto's List",b="When you return, Skuerto counts the wand as one item found. Three more remain on his list, and all three are in Stromgarde.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Wand over Fist?",a="At Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands, Skuerto asks you to recover the wand.",al={"wand over fist questgiver","who starts wand over fist","where to get wand over fist"}},{q="Where is Kor'gresh located?",a="Kor'gresh is in Boulderfist Hall, south of Refuge Pointe and then east of Thandol Span.",al={"where is korgresh","korgresh location","find korgresh"}},{q="What item needs to be recovered?",a="Trelane's Wand of Invocation is the first of Trelane's items to be recovered. Kor'gresh has used it to throw blasts of ice at his kin.",al={"what item is kor'gresh holding","what wand","trelane wand"}},{q="What prerequisites are needed for this quest?",a="You reach this work after Worth Its Weight in Gold, the work you did for Apprentice Kryten.",al={"wand over fist pre reqs","prerequisites for wand over fist","previous quest to wand over fist"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist hall","korgresh","refuge pointe","skuerto","stromgarde","thandol span","trelane","wand of invocation","wand over fist"},rel={"npc:skuerto","subzone:boulderfist-hall","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:thandol-span","zone:arathi"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=693},src={"Wand over Fist (Classic)"}}
E["quest:694"] = {t="quest",n="Trelane's Defenses",z="arathi",s="Ogres now ring the Tower of Arathor, and Skuerto needs its defenses working. An azure agate from the Boulderfist shaman can become a key after Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe enchants it.",h="Ogres now ring the Tower of Arathor, and Skuerto needs its defenses working.",sec={{t="The Tower's Defenses",b="In Stromgarde, ogres ring the Tower of Arathor. Skuerto says you need to activate its defenses to have a chance against them. Only then can you reach the items alive.",sp=0},{t="A Gem for a Key",b="The Boulderfist shaman took certain gems from the tower and have grown fond of them. Skuerto says they will not keep the gems for long. Bring an azure agate to Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe. Kryten knows the spell that will enchant it to work as a key.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is an azure agate needed?",a="Skuerto wants the tower's defenses active so you can face the ogres around the Tower of Arathor and reach the items alive. Enchanted, the gem will work as a key.",al={"why azure agate","trelane defenses purpose","why get the gem"}},{q="Where did the azure agates come from?",a="The Boulderfist shaman took the azure agates from the Tower of Arathor and have grown fond of them.",al={"who took the agates","where are the gems from","agate origin"}},{q="Who can enchant the gem?",a="Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe knows the spell to enchant the gem so it works as a key.",al={"who enchants the agate","kryten role","who turns it into a key"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","azure agate","boulderfist shaman","refuge pointe","skuerto","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane's defenses"},rel={"npc:skuerto","quest:695","subzone:tower-of-arathor","subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","topic:shaman"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Apprentice Kryten",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=694},src={"Trelane's Defenses (Classic)"}}
E["quest:695"] = {t="quest",n="An Apprentice's Enchantment",z="arathi",s="At the camp, Apprentice Kryten enchants the agate you brought from the Boulderfist shaman. It can wake the tower's defenses, and Kryten sends you to Skuerto before you leave.",h="At the camp, Apprentice Kryten enchants the agate you brought from the Boulderfist shaman.",sec={{t="A Key for the Tower",b="Apprentice Kryten gives you the enchanted gem and explains its power. Touch it to a pedestal at the tower's foot, and its defenses will wake. When you are ready to enter and search for the rest of Trelane's items, use the gem. Kryten will wait for you at the camp. Before you go, speak with Skuerto, who can answer any other questions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the enchanted agate?",a="Touch the enchanted agate to a pedestal at the tower's foot, and it wakes the tower's defenses. Use it when you are ready to enter and search for the rest of Trelane's items.",al={"why do i need the agate","enchanted agate use","what does the gem do"}},{q="Who do you need to talk to before leaving camp?",a="Speak to Skuerto before you leave the camp. Kryten says Skuerto can answer any other questions.",al={"who do i talk to","where to go next","who is skuerto"}},{q="Where will Kryten be?",a="Kryten will wait for your return at the camp.",al={"where is kryten","kryten waiting"}}},kw={"apprentice kryten","arathi highlands","enchanted agate","skuerto","tower","trelane"},rel={"npc:skuerto","zone:arathi"},m={start="Apprentice Kryten",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=695},src={"An Apprentice's Enchantment"}}
E["quest:696"] = {t="quest",n="Attack on the Tower",z="arathi",s="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto sends you to search the ogre-held tower for three items tied to Trelane. The phylactery, orb and ember agate should be in chests inside, and Skuerto says Malin will be pleased when you return with them.",h="At Refuge Pointe, Skuerto sends you to search the ogre-held tower for three items tied to Trelane.",sec={{t="Into the Tower",b="After Kryten enchants the gem, Skuerto sends you to find Trelane's phylactery, orb and ember agate. The three items should be in chests inside the tower, ready for you to open. But the ogres are dangerous. The tower's defenses will not deal with them, and the ogres will hurt you if they catch you stealing.",sp=0},{t="Skuerto's Verdict",b="When you return with the three items, Skuerto says Malin could not have asked for a worthier person to help them here. Malin will be delighted to learn their venture has succeeded so completely.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who assigns this task?",a="Skuerto sends you from Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands after Kryten enchants the gem.",al={"who gives attack on the tower","quest giver attack on the tower","where to get attack on the tower"}},{q="What items are you sent to retrieve?",a="You are sent to retrieve Trelane's phylactery, orb and ember agate. Each should be in a chest inside the tower.",al={"attack on the tower items","what relics to get","trelanes items"}},{q="What will the ogres do?",a="The tower's defenses will not deal with the ogres. If they catch you stealing, they will hurt you.",al={"are the ogres dangerous","tower ogres"}},{q="What comes before this?",a="It follows An Apprentice's Enchantment, where Kryten enchants the gem and sends you to Skuerto.",al={"attack on the tower prerequisite","what quest comes first"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","attack on the tower","malin","ogres","refuge pointe","skuerto","trelane","trelane's ember agate","trelane's orb","trelane's phylactery"},rel={"npc:skuerto","subzone:refuge-pointe","quest:695","zone:arathi"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Skuerto",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=696},src={"Attack on the Tower (Classic)"}}
E["quest:697"] = {t="quest",n="Malin's Request",z="arathi",s="In Stormwind, Skuerto's letter carries news from Arathi to Archmage Malin. You are sent to the Mage Quarter with word that Kryten and Skuerto will soon be home.",h="In Stormwind, Skuerto's letter carries news from Arathi to Archmage Malin.",sec={{t="A Letter for the Archmage",b="After your work in Arathi, Skuerto gives you a sealed letter for Archmage Malin in Stormwind's Mage Quarter. It says Kryten and Skuerto will be home soon. Skuerto trusts Malin will repay you well for helping them and wishes you a safe journey.",sp=0},{t="Malin Reads the Letter",b="Archmage Malin opens Skuerto's letter, and his eyes grow wide. Delighted, he says Trelane will be pleased. Malin supposes Kryten and Skuerto share his excitement as they head home to Stormwind.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you with the letter?",a="Skuerto sends you with a letter for Malin. It says Kryten and Skuerto will be home soon.",al={"who gives the letter","who starts malins request","malins request starter"}},{q="Where is Archmage Malin located?",a="Archmage Malin is in Stormwind's Mage Quarter.",al={"where is archmage malin","archmage malin location","where do i turn this in"}},{q="Who is Kryten?",a="Kryten is Skuerto's companion in the Arathi Highlands. Skuerto says they will be home soon.",al={"who is kryten","kryten arathi"}},{q="What comes before this step?",a="This follows Attack on the Tower, the work Skuerto asked you to do at the tower in Arathi.",al={"previous quest","prereq","what leads to this"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","kryten","mage quarter","malin's request","sealed letter","skuerto","stormwind"},rel={"npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","subzone:mage-quarter","zone:arathi","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:mage"},m={start="Skuerto",["end"]="Archmage Malin",level="39",faction="Alliance",id=697},src={"Malin's Request (2)"}}
E["quest:702"] = {t="quest",n="Guile of the Raptor",z="arathi",s="At Hammerfall, Tor'gan sends you to Gor'mul with an orb to rouse the warrior's spirit. Its energy bears the raptor's essence and may give Gor'mul fresh purpose.",h="At Hammerfall, Tor'gan sends you to Gor'mul with an orb to rouse the warrior's spirit.",sec={{t="Tor'gan's Orb",b="Tor'gan gives you an orb meant to fill Gor'mul with the raptor's essence. He hopes it will rouse the warrior's spirit and set him on a fresh course in life.\n\nOnce Gor'mul is himself again, Tor'gan plans to explain the Horde's present state. He hopes to win the help of a great warrior in its unceasing battles.",sp=0},{t="Gor'mul's Bitterness",b="Gor'mul greets your return with bitterness. He says all he wants is more of Tor'gan's pity, then mocks you with talk of brightly colored string.",sp=0},{t="A Strange Power",b="The orb draws Gor'mul's interest. He remarks on the strange power it gives off.",sp=1},{t="The Raptor Within",b="As Gor'mul takes the orb, his blood stirs and the raptor's guile slips through him. He wonders aloud if this is the shamanism Tor'gan spoke of. Then he declares himself renewed, with his strength returning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gor'mul?",a="At Hammerfall, Gor'mul is a despondent warrior. Tor'gan hopes to lift his spirits and set him on a new course, so the Horde can gain the aid of a great warrior.",al={"who is gormul","gormul lore","what is wrong with gormul"}},{q="What is the purpose of Tor'gan's Orb?",a="Tor'gan's Orb bears energy meant to fill Gor'mul with the raptor's essence. It may rouse his spirit and give him fresh purpose.",al={"what does the orb do","torgan orb purpose","guile orb"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="An earlier Guile of the Raptor comes first. This step builds on what happened there.",al={"previous quest","prereq"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","gor'mul","hammerfall","raptor essence","tor'gan","torgan's orb"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","quest:701","zone:arathi","topic:horde","topic:warrior"},m={start="Tor'gan",["end"]="Gor'mul",level="37",faction="Horde",id=702},src={"Guile of the Raptor (2)"}}
E["quest:847"] = {t="quest",n="Guile of the Raptor",z="arathi",s="Tor'gan's orb has filled Gor'mul with a raptor's essence. The power makes him wonder about shaman magic, and he will hear Tor'gan out for now.",h="Tor'gan's orb has filled Gor'mul with a raptor's essence.",sec={{t="A Warrior Convinced",b="Power runs through Gor'mul, and he wonders if it is the shamans' power Tor'gan tried to show him. The thought interests him. So he asks you to tell Tor'gan he is convinced for now and will hear what Tor'gan has to say.",sp=0},{t="Tor'gan's Reply",b="Tor'gan will speak with Gor'mul once the enchantment wears off. He thanks you for helping bring Gor'mul back among the living. Gor'mul is grateful too, Tor'gan believes.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends you to speak with Tor'gan?",a="Gor'mul sends you to speak with Tor'gan. After feeling the orb's power, he asks you to say he is convinced for now.",al={"who starts guile of the raptor 3","who gives this quest","where does this start"}},{q="Why does Gor'mul change his mind about Tor'gan?",a="Gor'mul wonders whether the power he felt came from the shamans, as Tor'gan tried to show him. The thought interests him, so he is convinced for now and will listen to Tor'gan.",al={"why did gormul change his mind","gormul shaman magic","is gormul convinced"}},{q="What came before this step?",a="You brought Tor'gan's orb to Gor'mul in the earlier step.",al={"previous quest","prereq guile of the raptor"}}},kw={"arathi highlands","gor'mul","guile of the raptor","hammerfall","shaman","tor'gan"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","topic:shaman","zone:arathi"},m={start="Gor'mul",["end"]="Tor'gan",level="37",faction="Horde",id=847},src={"Guile of the Raptor (3)"}}
E["subzone:boulder-gor"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulder'gor",z="arathi",s="Boulder'gor commands western Arathi, north of Stromgarde, where Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls share an encampment.",h="Boulder'gor commands western Arathi, north of Stromgarde, where Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls share...",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres and Trolls",b="North of Stromgarde Keep’s crumbling ramparts, Boulder'gor rises above the central roads of Arathi. The Boulderfist Outpost mound stands among its shadows, a stronghold of ogre power across the highlands. Boulderfist ogres share fires and fortifications with Witherbark forest trolls. Their shadowy spellcasters add dark magic to the clan’s brute force, and together they endanger travelers on the roads.",sp=0},{t="Surrounding Territory",b="From Boulder'gor’s slopes, you can look across the open highlands of western Arathi. The hill lies between Stromgarde’s Syndicate-infiltrated ruins and the plains’ wild elemental sites. Heavily guarded and hostile, Boulder'gor remains a tribal stronghold against Alliance and Horde wanderers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor rises as a hill and encampment north of Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands. Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls hold it in force.",al={"where is bouldergor","bouldergor info","what is this place"}},{q="Why are forest trolls living alongside ogres here?",a="The Witherbark trolls and Boulderfist ogres maintain a pragmatic alliance in Arathi. Both seek dominance over the highlands and aim to fend off rival factions, joining troll shadowcraft with brute ogre strength.",al={"why are trolls here","witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and ogres"}},{q="What major landmarks are near Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor lies directly north of Stromgarde Keep. Boulderfist Outpost’s ogre mound stands within the hill.",al={"nearby places","what is next to bouldergor","landmarks"}},{q="Is Boulder'gor friendly to the Horde or Alliance?",a="Neither faction is welcome. Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls aggressively defend Boulder'gor from Alliance and Horde outsiders.",al={"can i go there safely","is bouldergor hostile"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you will find no kinship with the Witherbark forest trolls of Boulder'gor. They hold ancient grudges against outsiders, even other troll tribes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier seeking to reclaim Stromgarde, you face a serious threat at Boulder'gor, on the fallen kingdom’s northern doorstep."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulder'gor","boulderfist","bouldergor","ogres","stromgarde","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulderfist-outpost","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulder'gor"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Hall",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist ogres hold the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, north of Thandol Span. Under Kor'gresh Coldrage, they threaten the nearby roads and valleys.",h="Boulderfist ogres hold the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, north of Thandol Span.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Brute Strength",b="Boulderfist Hall shelters the Boulderfist clan in the southern bluffs of the Arathi Highlands. Its earthen walls and deep caverns house ogre brutes and magi, near Witherbark Village and the bridge at Thandol Span. Kor'gresh Coldrage leads the clan from deep within the mound, with enforcers such as Phalanax at his side. The ogres hold the surrounding roads by force, making travel between Arathi and the Wetlands dangerous for travelers and supply caravans.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulderfist Hall?",a="Boulderfist Hall is a fortified mound and cave complex in the southern Arathi Highlands. The Boulderfist clan makes its base there.",al={"what is this place","boulderfist mound","ogre cave arathi"}},{q="Who rules Boulderfist Hall?",a="Kor'gresh Coldrage leads the ogres from a deep cavern in the mound. Champions such as Phalanax stand beside him.",al={"who leads boulderfist hall","ogre boss arathi","kor'gresh"}},{q="Why is this location strategically important?",a="Close to Thandol Span, the Boulderfist ogres can threaten the overland route between the Arathi Highlands and Khaz Modan. They prey on travelers and choke off traffic.",al={"why ogres here","thandol span danger"}},{q="Are the Boulderfist allied with the nearby Witherbark trolls?",a="No formal alliance binds the Boulderfist ogres and the Witherbark forest trolls. They live near one another at Witherbark Village, and at Boulder'gor elsewhere in the highlands, Witherbark trolls share ground with ogres. Both groups remain hostile to outsiders of every faction.",al={"ogres and trolls friends","witherbark alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Above Thandol Span, Boulderfist ogres threaten Alliance couriers and reinforcements traveling north from Ironforge into Arathi.",["faction:Horde"]="To secure the Arathi Highlands, you must break the ogres' independent power and clear the southern ridge. That protects Horde movement from Hammerfall."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist hall","kor'gresh coldrage","ogre mound","phalanax","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:witherbark-village"},src={"Boulderfist Hall"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Outpost",z="arathi",s="Deep within Boulder'gor, Boulderfist ogres hold a fortified mound and its inner halls. A few Witherbark trolls dwell among them in the Arathi Highlands.",h="Deep within Boulder'gor, Boulderfist ogres hold a fortified mound and its inner halls.",sec={{t="A Stronghold within the Mound",b="Boulderfist Outpost lies at the heart of Boulder'gor in western Arathi. Brute enforcers rule the settlement above, while the clan's strength gathers inside the mound. Carved from earth and stone, its dark halls serve as a den and a holding place. A few Witherbark troll witch doctors live among the ogres, a sign that the tribes sometimes share this ground.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderfist Outpost located?",a="Boulderfist Outpost lies within Boulder'gor, the larger ogre settlement in the western Arathi Highlands.",al={"boulderfist outpost location","where is boulderfist outpost","boulderfist mound entrance"}},{q="Why are there trolls inside an ogre outpost?",a="Witherbark forest trolls dwell nearby in the Arathi Highlands and sometimes share ground with the Boulderfist ogres. A few Witherbark witch doctors practice their craft inside the mound alongside them.",al={"why are witherbark here","trolls in boulderfist","witherbark trolls arathi"}},{q="Who is imprisoned in the outpost?",a="No named captives are known to be held in the outpost today. Boulderfist enforcers and a few Witherbark witch doctors occupy its damp corridors, where intruders should expect a fight rather than a rescue.",al={"boulderfist prisoners","who is trapped in boulderfist","captives in arathi ogres"}},{q="Who leads the ogres inside the outpost?",a="Boulderfist brute enforcers patrol the interior. An exceptionally fierce ogre named Kovork lurks within the mound as a notable threat.",al={"kovork","boulderfist boss arathi","boulderfist rare"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts crossing Arathi should give the mound a wide berth. Boulderfist enforcers attack intruders on sight.",["faction:Horde"]="Boulderfist ogres make no distinction between factions. They attack Horde wanderers as readily as their Alliance rivals."},kw={"arathi","boulder'gor","boulderfist","captives","kovork","ogre mound","prisoners","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulder-gor","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulderfist Outpost"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-east-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of East Binding",z="arathi",s="In eastern Arathi, water elementals guard the Circle of East Binding, southwest of Hammerfall. At its heart, the Stone of East Binding draws fierce contest.",h="In eastern Arathi, water elementals guard the Circle of East Binding, southwest of Hammerfall.",sec={{t="The Eastern Ward",b="East of Stromgarde, the Circle of East Binding lies among Arathi's rugged highlands. The Stone of East Binding rises at its center, charged with elemental magic. Cresting exiles roam the ground around it. These swirling water elementals fiercely defend the stone from any mortal who approaches.",sp=0},{t="Elemental Imprisonment",b="Ancient stones across Arathi bind volatile elemental forces. Around the eastern circle, restless water spirits show the strain on those wards. Drawn to the stone's magic or trapped by it, they lash out at travelers on the nearby road to Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Circle of East Binding located?",a="The Circle of East Binding lies in eastern Arathi, south of the main road and southwest of Hammerfall, the Horde camp.",al={"east binding location","where is circle of east binding","circle of east binding map"}},{q="What creatures are found here?",a="Aggressive water elementals called cresting exiles roam the circle and guard the Stone of East Binding.",al={"east binding mobs","what monsters are at east binding","cresting exiles"}},{q="Why are there water elementals in the highlands?",a="Ancient stones across Arathi bind elemental forces. The water elementals here may be held by the eastern ward stone or drawn to its energy.",al={"why water elementals arathi","east binding elemental lore"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Stone of East Binding?",a="The Stone of East Binding belongs to a network of binding stones across the Arathi Highlands. They were built to anchor, channel, and imprison volatile elemental forces.",al={"stone of east binding purpose","what does east binding stone do"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may see Arathi's binding stones as an ancient way to suppress elemental forces, far from the balance and communion you seek.",["faction:Horde"]="Just down the road from Hammerfall, volatile water spirits around the circle trouble Horde patrols and supply lines."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of east binding","cresting exile","elementals","hammerfall","stone of east binding"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall"},src={"Circle of East Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-inner-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of Inner Binding",z="arathi",s="Beneath the Arathi Highlands, the Circle of Inner Binding holds Myzrael beneath ancient stones. The Stone of Inner Binding anchors the strongest ward, but cracks let the imprisoned princess reach out to wanderers.",h="Beneath the Arathi Highlands, the Circle of Inner Binding holds Myzrael beneath ancient stones.",sec={{t="The Core Seal",b="South of the main road, towering slabs ring the Stone of Inner Binding on a plateau. The stone thrums with the strongest ward beneath Arathi and its dense geo-magical power. Rumbling Exiles patrol the stones, drawn by the site's resonance or bound there as guardians.\n\nCracks in the inner seal let the imprisoned Myzrael reach out telepathically. She whispers pleas for freedom to unsuspecting wanderers who handle shards of her stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Circle of Inner Binding?",a="The Circle holds the Stone of Inner Binding, the strongest ward anchoring Myzrael's prison beneath the earth. It works with other elemental circles scattered through the Arathi Highlands to restrain her below the surface.",al={"why is this circle here","what does the inner binding do","circle of inner binding lore"}},{q="What creatures guard this circle?",a="Powerful earth elementals guard the circle, chiefly Rumbling Exiles. These rocky behemoths attack anyone who approaches the ritual stones.",al={"what enemies are here","inner binding mobs","rumbling exile"}},{q="Who is whispering through the stone?",a="Myzrael is an ancient and powerful elemental princess imprisoned deep beneath the earth. Her psychic reach has pierced the fractured seal, letting her contact mortal minds through the binding shard.",al={"who talks to you here","myzrael voice","whispering stone"}},{q="Where is the Circle of Inner Binding located?",a="The Circle stands on an elevated ridgeline in the southern Arathi Highlands, just east of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"inner binding location","where is circle of inner binding","how to find inner binding"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can feel raw earthen energy surging through the Circle of Inner Binding. Its ancient, heavy elemental bonds are clear, while the earth spirits' unnatural agitation warns of corruption beneath the soil.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can read an intricate pattern in the stones. Their geometric arrangement forms a lasting containment field that channels and anchors immense subterranean magical pressures."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of inner binding","earth elementals","myzrael","rumbling exile","stone of inner binding","stromgarde keep"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep"},src={"Circle of Inner Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-west-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of West Binding",z="arathi",s="Near Thoradin's Wall, Burning Exiles overrun the Circle of West Binding and guard its stone. The ancient ritual site is one of several scattered across the Arathi Highlands.",h="Near Thoradin's Wall, Burning Exiles overrun the Circle of West Binding and guard its stone.",sec={{t="The Western Keystone",b="Near Thoradin's Wall, the Stone of West Binding stands at the Circle of West Binding. The site belongs to a wider network of ancient ritual places scattered across the Arathi Highlands. Burning Exiles overrun the grounds and guard the stone. Their fiery presence makes an approach perilous for travelers crossing the western plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Circle of West Binding?",a="The Circle of West Binding is an ancient ritual site in western Arathi Highlands, near Thoradin's Wall. The Stone of West Binding stands there, guarded by hostile fire elementals.",al={"circle of west binding","stone of west binding","west binding circle"}},{q="Why are there fire elementals here?",a="The Burning Exiles inhabit and guard the Stone of West Binding. These elemental forces are drawn or bound to ancient magical foci built across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"burning exiles arathi","why fire elementals west binding","elementals circle of west binding"}},{q="Who is Ruul Onestone?",a="Ruul Onestone is a Boulderfist ogre mage who prowls the site. He is a rare and dangerous brute, not a scholar of the binding stone.",al={"ruul onestone","ruul","dwarf at west binding"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can find insight in Arathi's binding stones into how ancient mages and shamans anchored and subdued planar elemental entities.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can read the Burning Exiles' volatile presence as a sign of elemental unrest still tethered to these ancient Arathi keystones."},kw={"arathi highlands","burning exile","circle of west binding","elemental","ruul onestone","stone of west binding","thoradin's wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thoradin-s-wall"},src={"Circle of West Binding"}}
E["subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="In Stromgarde Keep, loyalists guard the royal crypt beneath the Sanctum. It holds King Thoras Trollbane’s tomb and the treasures of his line.",h="In Stromgarde Keep, loyalists guard the royal crypt beneath the Sanctum.",sec={{t="The Tomb of Thoras Trollbane",b="Beneath Stromgarde Keep’s Sanctum lies King Thoras Trollbane’s tomb. He led Stromgarde through the Second War. The city is in ruins, divided between Syndicate rogues and Boulderfist ogres, yet the surviving Stromgarde militia still holds this quarter.\n\nPrince Galen Trollbane watches over the crypt with the royal caretakers. They keep his father’s body and legacy safe from scavengers and enemies outside.",sp=0},{t="The Vault of Trol'kalar",b="The crypt guards artifacts of the Trollbane line. Among them is Trol'kalar, an ancient runed greatsword forged centuries ago to slay trolls. Sworn caretakers, including Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston, protect the chamber and its treasures with powerful safeguards.\n\nGalen and his loyalists keep watch. Rival factions and hostile trolls across Arathi covet the blade’s ancient power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is buried in the crypt?",a="King Thoras Trollbane, Stromgarde’s late ruler, is buried in the crypt. His son, Prince Galen Trollbane, watches over the tomb amid the ruined city.",al={"who is buried here","whose tomb is this","crypt tomb"}},{q="What is Trol'kalar?",a="Trol'kalar is an ancient heirloom blade of the Trollbane family. Its name means “troll slayer” in the ancient tongue. It was forged to fight the forest trolls of the Arathi basin.",al={"trolkalar sword","trollbane sword","what is trolkalar"}},{q="Who guards the crypt?",a="Prince Galen Trollbane and Stromgarde’s royal caretakers guard the crypt, including Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston. They defend the burial chamber from Syndicate thieves and Boulderfist ogres.",al={"crypt guards","who defends the crypt","caretakers"}},{q="Where is the crypt located?",a="The crypt lies within Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands, deep in the Sanctum district behind the keep’s chapel. It is in the quarter still held by Stromgarde loyalists.",al={"crypt location","how to find the crypt","where is stromgarde crypt"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the Alliance, you can see Stromgarde’s decline in this tomb. Here rests one of the Alliance’s fiercest wartime leaders, from one of its seven great kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you find one of Arathi’s last bastions of Alliance heritage in Stromgarde’s royal crypt. Its defenders hold off bandits, ogres, and the Horde."},kw={"arathi","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","thoras","trol'kalar","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi"},src={"Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:dabyrie-s-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Dabyrie's Farmstead",z="arathi",s="In northern Arathi, the Dabyries keep their farm against the dangers around them. Kenata Dabyrie holds fast with her sons, loyal to Stromgarde and the Alliance in a realm broken by the Third War.",h="In northern Arathi, the Dabyries keep their farm against the dangers around them.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Highlands",b="Kenata Dabyrie and her sons hold their farm against the dangers around them. Fardel and Marcel work the fields while a local family militia guards the grounds. Few human homesteads still endure in the broken kingdom of Stromgarde. Aggressive wildlife and bandits threaten the farm, and the Forsaken press from the north. The Dabyries keep their home in a land where few human settlements remain.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Feuds",b="The Forsaken have turned against the Dabyries, and Genavie Callow is among their bitterest foes. Once a noblewoman, Callow lost her lands and kin during the Third War. She accuses the surviving Dabyrie family of taking her family's heirlooms amid the plague's chaos. Now Horde mercenaries target the modest farm to settle old grudges from the north.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dabyrie's Farmstead?",a="Kenata Dabyrie lives at the farm with her sons, Fardel and Marcel. They are human citizens of Stromgarde, loyal to the Alliance and defended by a sworn local militia.",al={"who owns dabyrie farm","dabyrie family","kenata dabyrie"}},{q="Why is the Horde targeting this farm?",a="The Forsaken woman Genavie Callow holds a grudge against the Dabyries. She accuses them of taking her family's estate and surviving heirlooms while her relatives perished in the Third War.",al={"why kill dabyrie","genavie callow quest","horde dabyrie quest"}},{q="Is Dabyrie's Farmstead part of Stromgarde?",a="Yes. The Dabyries consider themselves subjects of Stromgarde and allies of the broader Alliance, though their capital lies in ruins to the south.",al={"is dabyrie alliance","stromgarde farm"}},{q="What threats surround the farmstead?",a="Highland predators and roaming Syndicate cutthroats threaten the farm. Forsaken forces press from the north.",al={"threats to dabyrie","danger near dabyrie farm"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find a rare reminder here that Stromgarde's people still survive and fight for their land amid encroaching enemies.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see a prosperous human farm holding goods your people say were taken from families who perished during the Third War."},kw={"arathi","callow","dabyrie","fardel","farmstead","kenata","marcel","stromgarde"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","topic:syndicate"},src={"Dabyrie's Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:drowned-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Drowned Reef",z="arathi",s="Ships bound for Faldir's Cove risk the Drowned Reef off Arathi's southern coast. Ancient ruins lie below, where Daggerspine naga seem able to command the bay's tides.",h="Ships bound for Faldir's Cove risk the Drowned Reef off Arathi's southern coast.",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships",b="Beyond the hidden entrance to Faldir's Cove, shattered ships rest beneath the waves. The Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine lie among them. Daggerspine naga dwell on the reef under Prince Nazjak's command. They seem able to command the bay's tides, and crews seeking shelter in the cove may be doomed by them.",sp=0},{t="The Sunken City",b="Deep beneath the reef lie the ruins of an ancient elven city. Dive among the drowned buildings, and calcified elven gems can still be found among the remains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Drowned Reef?",a="The Drowned Reef lies off the southern coast of the Arathi Highlands, just offshore from Faldir's Cove. Its waters endanger ships, while ancient ruins lie beneath the sea.",al={"drowned reef","where is drowned reef","arathi reef"}},{q="Why are there so many sunken ships here?",a="Ships face danger in the waters off Arathi's southern coast. Daggerspine naga seem able to command the bay's tides, putting crews seeking refuge in Faldir's Cove at risk.",al={"why are ships sinking","sunken ships arathi","maidens folly"}},{q="Who controls the Drowned Reef?",a="Daggerspine naga inhabit the Drowned Reef's flooded ruins under Prince Nazjak's command. They prey on stranded sailors and guard their submerged territory.",al={"who leads the naga here","prince nazjak","daggerspine naga arathi"}},{q="What are the ruins submerged beneath the reef?",a="The ruins beneath the Drowned Reef belong to an ancient elven city. Calcified elven gems remain among its drowned buildings.",al={"underwater ruins arathi","elven ruins drowned reef"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a Night Elf, you may see the flooded halls and calcified gems as reminders of the Kaldorei empire. It shattered into the sea ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering."},kw={"arathi highlands","daggerspine","drowned reef","faldir's cove","maiden's folly","naga","prince nazjak","spirit of silverpine","sunken ruins"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:faldir-s-cove","topic:naga"},src={"Drowned Reef"}}
E["subzone:drywhisker-gorge"] = {t="subzone",n="Drywhisker Gorge",z="arathi",s="Northeast of Hammerfall, Drywhisker kobolds hold a gorge in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands. They guard its inner cavern, rich mineral deposits and ancient elemental relics buried underground.",h="Northeast of Hammerfall, Drywhisker kobolds hold a gorge in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Warren in the Eastern Crags",b="Drywhisker kobolds hold the crags east of Hammerfall. Their clan has dug deep into the mountains and fiercely guards its winding passages. Below, they mine veins of Lesser Bloodstone Ore. Their stronghold lies close enough to trouble the orcs at Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Deep Cavern",b="Deep in the Drywhisker cavern lies a stone shard. The kobolds are allied with the towering stone giants of the highlands and tend motes of ancient earth magic. The shard holds a trapped fragment of Princess Myzrael's essence. She is an ancient earth entity bound below the surface.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Drywhisker Gorge?",a="The Drywhisker clan of kobolds lives in the gorge and its cavern passages. They defend their territory and mining operations, along with the relics hidden within.",al={"drywhisker gorge inhabitants","what is in drywhisker gorge","who controls drywhisker gorge"}},{q="Where is Drywhisker Gorge located?",a="Drywhisker Gorge cuts through the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, northeast of Hammerfall. A rugged path climbs through the hills east of the outpost to the cavern entrance.",al={"how to get to drywhisker gorge","drywhisker gorge location","where is the cave in arathi"}},{q="What makes the cave inside significant?",a="The cave holds rare deposits of Lesser Bloodstone Ore and an ancient stone shard. The shard contains a fragment of Princess Myzrael's imprisoned essence.",al={"what is in the cave","drywhisker cave secrets","myzrael shard"}},{q="Why are the kobolds allied with mountain giants?",a="The Drywhisker clan is allied with the local stone giants. The kobolds serve and guard earth relics and elemental motes tied to Princess Myzrael's bindings deep beneath Arathi.",al={"kobolds and giants","why are drywhiskers with giants"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners prize the Drywhisker cavern as the only known source of Lesser Bloodstone Ore. The dense, crimson-veined mineral lies deep within the kobold-held rock.",["faction:Horde"]="The hostile Drywhisker kobolds live just over the mountain ridge east of Hammerfall. They threaten the outpost's eastern flank."},kw={"arathi highlands","drywhisker","drywhisker gorge","hammerfall","kobold","lesser bloodstone ore","princess myzrael","stone shard"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:kobold"},src={"Drywhisker Gorge"}}
E["subzone:faldir-s-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Faldir's Cove",z="arathi",s="Blackwater Raiders now shelter at Faldir's Cove after disaster struck their fleet on the Arathi coast. The harbor also recalls the early settlers who sailed south from here to found Stormwind.",h="Blackwater Raiders now shelter at Faldir's Cove after disaster struck their fleet on the Arathi coast.",sec={{t="A Gateway South and a Pirate Haven",b="South of Stromgarde Keep, Faldir's Cove lies behind the bluffs, reached through a hidden tunnel beneath the ground. The harbor bears the name of Faldir, an ancient Arathor explorer whose expedition sailed across the Great Sea to establish Stormwind. Now Blackwater Raiders from Booty Bay shelter in its waters. Captains Steelgut and O'Breen led them north in search of ancient elven treasures, but their expedition became trapped in the bay.",sp=0},{t="The Wreck of the Blackwater Fleet",b="The Blackwater expedition met disaster on the Arathi coast. Unnatural tides, stirred by territorial naga on the offshore Drowned Reef, shattered two of their three ships. Only the Harbinger reached Faldir's Cove intact. With naga prowling the waters and their navigation charts lost beneath the waves, the surviving pirates and gnomish researchers are stranded. They rely on travelers to fight the aquatic horrors and recover salvage from the seabed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Faldir?",a="Faldir was an ancient pioneer from the human empire of Arathor. He and his followers sailed south from this coast across the sea to establish the settlements that became Stormwind.",al={"faldir lore","who is faldir","faldir founder"}},{q="How do you reach Faldir's Cove?",a="Reach Faldir's Cove through a hidden tunnel just southeast of Stromgarde Keep's outer southern walls. The passage runs beneath the ground and opens onto the secluded shore.",al={"how to get to faldir's cove","faldir cove entrance","cave to faldirs cove"}},{q="Why are the Blackwater Raiders here?",a="Captain Steelgut and Captain O'Breen led the Blackwater Raiders north from Booty Bay to seek sunken elven treasures. Gnomish inventors came with them, carrying devices designed to detect gems in the offshore reefs.",al={"why are pirates here","blackwater raiders arathi","what are the pirates doing"}},{q="What happened to their ships?",a="Hostile naga on the Drowned Reef stirred unnatural tides that destroyed two of the expedition's three vessels. The flagship Harbinger reached the cove, but the crew's charts sank beneath the waves.",al={"why are ships wrecked","sunken ships arathi","who sank the ships"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you stand on the coast where your ancestors left Arathor and sailed south toward the settlements that became Stormwind.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can find Doctor Draxlegauge and Professor Phizzlethorpe at the camp, using engineering devices to study and extract elven gems from the calcified coastal reefs."},kw={"blackwater raiders","captain o'breen","captain steelgut","draxlegauge","drowned reef","faldir","faldir's cove","harbinger","phizzlethorpe"},rel={"subzone:drowned-reef","zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:booty-bay","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:naga"},src={"Faldir's Cove"}}
E["subzone:go-shek-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Go'Shek Farm",z="arathi",s="Go'Shek Farm gathers food and livestock for Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands. Forsaken apothecaries also work there in secret.",h="Go'Shek Farm gathers food and livestock for Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Horde Outpost in the East",b="South of Hammerfall, Go'Shek Farm lies just north of hostile Witherbark troll territory. The Horde holds the farm, and Hammerfall Grunts patrol its fields and stables. Its food and livestock help the orcish settlement keep its foothold in the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="The Apothecary's Workshop",b="The Royal Apothecary Society keeps a quiet presence at Go'Shek Farm, led by figures such as Apothecary Jorell. Couriers carry notes, reagents, and research between the farm and Tarren Mill, studying early forms of the Forsaken's new plague. Alliance scouts seek to intercept the messengers and learn what poison is being prepared in the Arathi soil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde occupying Go'Shek Farm?",a="Go'Shek Farm supplies food and livestock to nearby Hammerfall. It also gives the Forsaken a guarded place for sensitive chemical and alchemical research.",al={"who owns goshek farm","why are orcs at goshek farm","goshek farm horde"}},{q="Who used to own this farm?",a="The farm's earlier owners are not recorded. Today, orcs from nearby Hammerfall work and guard it for the Horde.",al={"goshek farm history","human farm arathi","primwell skye"}},{q="What kind of experiments are happening here?",a="Forsaken apothecaries conduct secretive alchemical work at the farm. Alliance agents investigate courier traffic and records there to learn its nature.",al={"apothecary jorell","plague experiments arathi","forsaken research goshek"}},{q="Why are there Alliance agents watching the farm?",a="Quae and Kinelory investigate suspicious traffic between Go'Shek Farm and Tarren Mill. They seek evidence of the Forsaken's activities and need help reaching it.",al={"quae kinelory","alliance scouting goshek","hints of a new plague"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The farm supplies Hammerfall and houses Forsaken apothecaries whose secretive work has drawn Alliance scrutiny.",["faction:Horde"]="Keeping Go'Shek Farm secure helps provision Hammerfall and guard its perimeter against the encroaching Witherbark trolls."},kw={"apothecary jorell","arathi","go'shek farm","goshek","hammerfall","kinelory","quae","swee","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:367","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:witherbark-village","topic:alliance"},src={"Go'Shek Farm"}}
E["subzone:hammerfall"] = {t="subzone",n="Hammerfall",z="arathi",s="Horde forces hold Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, where old losses and a hard-won freedom shape the outpost. Orcs and Forsaken defend it against Boulderfist ogres, Witherbark trolls, and the League of Arathor.",h="Horde forces hold Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands, where old losses and a hard-won freedom shape the...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Liberation",b="Beneath Hammerfall lie the ruins of an Alliance internment camp. After the Second War, the human Alliance built vast camps across Lordaeron for defeated orcs, and this was among the largest. Years later, Thrall and Orgrim Doomhammer struck at the camp to free its lethargic captives.\n\nAs they retreated, an Alliance knight charged and drove a lance through Doomhammer's backplate. The Warchief was mortally wounded. After the Third War, the new Horde reclaimed the ruins and named its outpost Hammerfall in his memory.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold in the Highlands",b="Hammerfall gives the Horde a foothold in Arathi. Its garrison faces aggressive Boulderfist ogres from Boulder'gor and Boulderfist Hall, as well as the native Witherbark trolls. Forsaken Defilers use the outpost to claim resources in the contested Arathi Basin. There they oppose the Alliance's League of Arathor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this base called Hammerfall?",a="The base honors Orgrim Doomhammer, who was mortally wounded by an Alliance knight's lance while freeing orcs from the internment camp.",al={"why hammerfall","hammerfall name origin","who died at hammerfall"}},{q="What was Hammerfall before the Horde rebuilt it?",a="Before the Horde rebuilt it, the site held one of the largest Alliance of Lordaeron internment camps. It was built after the Second War to imprison captive orcs.",al={"hammerfall history","what was hammerfall before","internment camp arathi"}},{q="Who leads the defense of Hammerfall right now?",a="Orc Drum Fel rules Hammerfall and directs its defense against the Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls. Tallow, a Forsaken warrior at Tarren Mill, first sends recruits to attack the Boulderfist ogres of Boulder'gor.",al={"hammerfall leaders","who is in charge of hammerfall","tallow drum fel"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken stationed here?",a="Forsaken Defilers operate from Hammerfall to secure supplies from the Arathi Basin. They oppose the Alliance's League of Arathor.",al={"forsaken hammerfall","why are undead in hammerfall","defilers arathi"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs, Hammerfall is hallowed ground. Orgrim Doomhammer gave his life here freeing captive clanmates and passing the mantle of Warchief to Thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, Hammerfall is its fortress in the central Arathi Highlands. Hostile ogres, forest trolls, and remnants of the Alliance surround it."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","defilers","hammerfall","internment camp","orgrim doomhammer","thrall","witherbark"},rel={"npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:arathi","npc:thrall","npc:drum-fel","npc:tallow","subzone:boulder-gor","subzone:boulderfist-hall","topic:second-war"},src={"Hammerfall"}}
E["subzone:northfold-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Northfold Manor",z="arathi",s="The Syndicate holds Northfold Manor in northwestern Arathi. Once a prosperous human homestead, the estate fell into ruin after Stromgarde collapsed and now shelters criminals and dark practices.",h="The Syndicate holds Northfold Manor in northwestern Arathi.",sec={{t="A Den of Brigands",b="Near the passage through Thoradin's Wall, Northfold Manor spreads across the rolling highlands. The estate once supported the kingdom of Stromgarde. After the realm fractured, displaced Alteraci nobles and Syndicate outlaws claimed the manor house, barn, and fields as their base.\n\nMercenaries, highwaymen, and pathstalkers gather there, leaving the crops untended. From the farmstead, they ambush travelers on nearby roads and coordinate the Syndicate's presence across Arathi.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Undertones",b="Demonic summoning has marked Northfold Manor. Sensitive spellcasters and shamans in the region feel traces that linger across the grounds. Bloodstone amulets, potent talismans used to fuel dark invocations, lie discarded there. Their presence points to Syndicate rogues entangling themselves with demonic magic beyond ordinary banditry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Northfold Manor?",a="The Syndicate controls Northfold Manor and uses the estate as an armed encampment. Its ranks include dispossessed Alteraci nobles, bandits, and rogue mercenaries.",al={"who lives here","who owns northfold","syndicate farm"}},{q="What dark magic is being practiced here?",a="Those sensitive to magic can feel lingering traces of demonic summoning at Northfold Manor. Syndicate forces there possess bloodstone amulets that help channel dangerous demonic rituals.",al={"demons at northfold","bloodstone","what are they summoning"}},{q="Why does the Horde care about this farm?",a="At Hammerfall, the troll shaman Tor'gan sensed an unnatural disturbance brewing across the highlands. His search for its source led him to Northfold Manor, where the Horde now investigates the Syndicate's occult activities.",al={"horde interest northfold","why tor'gan cares"}},{q="Who is Singer?",a="Singer is an elusive Syndicate figure sometimes seen among the brigands inside Northfold Manor's main house.",al={"singer","singer rare","who is singer"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall's shamans keep watch over Northfold Manor. They send warriors to seize the bloodstone talismans the Syndicate uses in attempts at demonic summoning.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you may feel demonic residue around Northfold Manor disrupting the natural elements. It brings spiritual unease and fiery rage to shamans attuned to the elements."},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","northfold manor","singer","stromgarde","syndicate","tor'gan"},rel={"topic:syndicate","zone:arathi","topic:horde","quest:255","topic:troll"},src={"Northfold Manor"}}
E["subzone:refuge-pointe"] = {t="subzone",n="Refuge Pointe",z="arathi",s="Refuge Pointe holds its ground in the Arathi Highlands as Stromgarde's remnant prepares to reclaim its fallen keep. The camp guards the trade road at the highlands' heart while Alliance forces face rivals across the region.",h="Refuge Pointe holds its ground in the Arathi Highlands as Stromgarde's remnant prepares to reclaim its fallen...",sec={{t="A Bastion for Stromgarde's Remnants",b="Stromgarde's surviving soldiers hold Refuge Pointe. After the Third War and the fall of Stromgarde Keep, most of the kingdom's people fled south for safer lands. Those who stayed formed a vanguard under Captain Nials. Battle-hardened Stromgarde soldiers stand with League of Arathor forces and Alliance specialists. Together, they are the last organized Stromgarde force in its ancestral homeland.",sp=0},{t="Stretched to the Limit",b="Refuge Pointe has no reserves to spare. The Forsaken and Horde hold Hammerfall, while Witherbark trolls, Syndicate rogues, and Boulderfist ogres press the garrison from other sides. When dwarven commanders at battered Thandol Span asked for help against the Dark Iron clan, Captain Nials had to refuse.\n\nEvery soldier and supply at Refuge Pointe must defend the highlands and prepare to retake Stromgarde Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Alliance presence here so small?",a="Most of Stromgarde's surviving civilians fled south after the kingdom fell in the Third War. The small force at Refuge Pointe is a remnant of its army, joined by an Alliance expedition. With supplies stretched thin and enemies on every front, they struggle to hold their camp.",al={"why is refuge pointe small","why so few soldiers","alliance numbers arathi"}},{q="Why won't Refuge Pointe send soldiers to help at the Thandol Span?",a="Captain Nials refused the dwarves' request for troops to defend Dun Modr and Thandol Span from Dark Iron attacks. Stromgarde Keep is overrun, and hostile forces surround Refuge Pointe. Every soldier must help hold the highlands and prepare to reclaim the fallen capital.",al={"why no help dun modr","captain nials thandol span","plea to the alliance quest"}},{q="Who commands the camp?",a="Captain Nials commands Refuge Pointe's garrison. She directs Stromgarde's operations across the highlands, from scouting and skirmishes with the Syndicate and ogres to patrols along the main road.",al={"refuge pointe leader","who is in charge here","captain nials"}},{q="What is the League of Arathor?",a="The League of Arathor is an Alliance coalition seeking to reclaim the Arathi Highlands and secure resources in neighboring Arathi Basin. Its forces fight beside Stromgarde's remnant at Refuge Pointe to keep the Forsaken-led Defilers from controlling the fertile valley.",al={"league of arathor","who are league of arathor","arathi basin alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Refuge Pointe is your military sanctuary and flight hub in the Arathi Highlands. Here, you find relief in a territory contested by ogres, the Syndicate, and the Horde.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can look to Refuge Pointe and remember Stromgarde's former glory as humanity's martial heartland. Its defenders refuse to abandon their homeland despite overwhelming odds."},kw={"arathi highlands","arathor","captain nials","league of arathor","refuge pointe","stromgarde","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","topic:alliance","npc:longbraid-the-grim","npc:skuerto","topic:third-war"},src={"Refuge Pointe"}}
E["subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="Behind the chapel in Stromgarde Keep, the Sanctum remains a sacred refuge. It guards the way to the Trollbane family crypt amid Arathi's ruin.",h="Behind the chapel in Stromgarde Keep, the Sanctum remains a sacred refuge.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Ruins",b="Syndicate infiltrators and Boulderfist ogres have taken much of Stromgarde Keep. Yet defenders still hold the Sanctum and the chapel beside it. Behind the Church of Light, the Sanctum borders the keep's graveyard and marks the way into the royal crypt, where Stromgarde's kings rest. Prince Galen Trollbane's loyalists defend this ground to protect their kingdom's ancestral heritage and faith from the invaders.",sp=0},{t="Threshold of the Kings",b="Stone flags cover the passage into the royal tomb beneath the Sanctum. The ground is consecrated for quiet reflection and worship of the Holy Light. After King Thoras Trollbane's murder and Stromgarde's collapse, the Sanctum became a defensive retreat. Royal guards hold its halls against anyone seeking the inner tomb. At this sacred threshold, an ancient human lineage clings to survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sanctum?",a="The Sanctum lies behind the Church of Light's chapel within Stromgarde Keep. It adjoins the keep's graveyard and leads into the Trollbane family crypt.",al={"what is sanctum","stromgarde sanctum","sanctum stromgarde keep"}},{q="Who controls the Sanctum right now?",a="Surviving Stromgarde soldiers loyal to the Alliance and Prince Galen Trollbane hold the Sanctum. Human guards defend the chapel and Sanctum while Syndicate bandits and Boulderfist ogres overrun the rest of the ruined city.",al={"who is in the sanctum","sanctum guards","who holds the sanctum"}},{q="What lies beyond the Sanctum?",a="The Trollbane family crypt lies beyond the Sanctum. It holds Stromgarde's fallen rulers, including the recently slain King Thoras Trollbane.",al={"where does sanctum lead","sanctum crypt","what is behind the sanctum"}},{q="Why is this area important to Stromgarde?",a="The Sanctum is consecrated for worship of the Holy Light and guards the resting place of Stromgarde's kings. Its defenders fight to keep invaders from desecrating their ancestors' graves.",al={"why care about sanctum","sanctum significance","why is sanctum defended"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find the chapel and Sanctum among the last undefiled sanctuaries of the Holy Light in Arathi's fallen capital. Defending them is a solemn duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help hold the Trollbane ancestral seat and keep the Alliance presence alive in Stromgarde's contested ruins."},kw={"arathi","chapel","church of light","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Stromgarde Keep",z="arathi",s="In the Arathi Highlands, Stromgarde Keep is divided between its royal defenders, the Syndicate and Boulderfist ogres. The fallen kingdom's battered capital holds only part of its fortress.",h="In the Arathi Highlands, Stromgarde Keep is divided between its royal defenders, the Syndicate and...",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="Strom began as the first capital of the unified human empire of Arathor. King Thoradin founded it nearly three millennia ago. From this fortress, humanity prepared its victory over the forest trolls. Here, high elven magi taught the first hundred human spellcasters and began the long history of human wizardry.\n\nDalaran, Lordaeron and Stormwind rose as younger sister kingdoms while Strom's influence waned. The stubborn Trollbane dynasty remained and renamed the city Stromgarde. Through the Second War, it stood as a proud warrior bastion and an anchor of the Alliance of Lordaeron against the Orcish Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Bastion",b="The devastation of the Third War brought mounting disasters and treachery, and Stromgarde finally broke. Its majestic stone city is now split into three warring sectors. Aristocratic Syndicate traitors hold the grand inner keep, while Boulderfist ogres have overrun the former sanctum of the mage district.\n\nPrince Galen Trollbane and the battered Stromgarde military hold the remaining quarter. They wage a hard, bloody war on several fronts to keep their ancestral home from vanishing into memory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Stromgarde Keep right now?",a="Three warring forces divide the ruined city. The Syndicate holds the central inner keep, Boulderfist ogres occupy the ruined mage district, and Prince Galen Trollbane leads the surviving Stromgarde army from the remaining quarter.",al={"who lives in stromgarde","who owns stromgarde keep","who is in stromgarde"}},{q="What was the Empire of Arathor?",a="The Empire of Arathor was the first unified human nation, founded nearly three thousand years ago under King Thoradin. Its capital, Strom, stood where Stromgarde Keep now stands.",al={"what is strom","first human kingdom","arathor empire"}},{q="Why is the city in ruins?",a="Stromgarde's kingdom was left vulnerable and isolated in the chaos after the Third War. Betrayal within the city, attacks by the criminal Syndicate and assaults by Boulderfist ogres shattered its defenses.",al={"why is stromgarde destroyed","what happened to stromgarde"}},{q="Who is Galen Trollbane?",a="Prince Galen Trollbane is the royal scion and commander of Stromgarde's surviving forces. From his embattled redoubt inside the keep, he directs the desperate defense against the Syndicate and the ogres.",al={"prince trollbane","who is prince galen"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you can look to Stromgarde as the ancient heart of your race. The first human tribes united under Thoradin here, and high elves taught them the arcane arts. Seeing criminals and ogres overrun the city is a bitter sight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can look to Stromgarde, a founding member of the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. Its beleaguered defenders remain one of the last loyal strongholds in the north, fighting to avoid total ruin."},kw={"arathi","arathor","boulderfist","galen","strom","stromgarde","stromgarde keep","syndicate","thoradin","trollbane"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Stromgarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:thandol-span"] = {t="subzone",n="Thandol Span",z="arathi",s="At Thandol Span, the surviving bridge lies under attack. Its stone arches link the Wetlands of Khaz Modan with the Arathi Highlands of southern Lordaeron, but Dark Iron infiltrators have sabotaged one crossing.",h="At Thandol Span, the surviving bridge lies under attack.",sec={{t="The Fight for the Crossing",b="Ironforge Mountaineers guard the surviving bridge. They fight to hold the roadway and drive back Dark Iron sappers, though the defense costs them dearly. If the bridge falls, northern trade and military movements will rely almost entirely on sea routes. Alliance forces in the Arathi Highlands will lose their immediate reinforcement.",sp=0},{t="A Lifeline Severed",b="Dwarves built the Thandol Span after the War of the Three Hammers to link Ironforge with the Wildhammer clan at Aerie Peak. Its bridges rank among the grandest works of dwarven stonecraft, strong enough to bear entire marching armies. During the Second War, armies crossed between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan here, including Sir Anduin Lothar's counter-offensive south.\n\nNow Dark Iron saboteurs have struck from nearby Dun Modr. Led by Balgaras the Foul and Kam Deepfury, they used explosives to shatter one span and threaten the overland route between the allied realms.",sp=1,bt={"q303.3"}}},faq={{q="What is the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span carries you across a deep canyon between the Wetlands in northern Khaz Modan and the Arathi Highlands in southern Lordaeron. Dwarves built its two stone arches.",al={"thandol span overview","what is this bridge","thandol bridge"},it="place"},{q="Why is one of the bridges broken?",a="Dark Iron dwarves attacked from the captured outpost of Dun Modr. They used explosives to demolish one of the two spans and cut Alliance supply lines.",al={"who blew up the bridge","thandol span destroyed","why is thandol span broken"},it="ruin"},{q="Why was the Thandol Span originally built?",a="Ironforge dwarves built the Span after the War of the Three Hammers to strengthen trade, diplomacy, and ties with their Wildhammer cousins across the canyon in the north.",al={"who built thandol span","thandol history","why was it built"},it="origin"},{q="Did armies cross here during the Second War?",a="Yes. The Old Horde crossed the sea to invade Lordaeron. Later, Sir Anduin Lothar led the Alliance counter-offensive across the Span, driving the orcs back into Khaz Modan.",al={"thandol span second war","orcs at thandol span","lothar thandol span"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span is held and guarded by the dwarves of Ironforge. Despite suffering brutal raids and sabotage from Dark Iron infiltrators operating out of nearby Dun Modr, Ironforge mountaineers continue to defend the surviving bridge, keeping open the vital link between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms.",al={"who controls thandol span","who runs thandol span","thandol span guards"},it="residents",add="6e9af8e2"},{q="Is the Thandol Span dangerous?",a="Yes, traveling across the Span is hazardous. Dark Iron saboteurs recently infiltrated the gorge and detonated explosives, completely severing one of the two twin arches and leaving the remaining span vulnerable. Hostile Dark Iron dwarves linger nearby in the northern Wetlands and around Dun Modr, actively plotting further strikes against travelers and Ironforge defenders holding the line.",al={"is thandol span safe","thandol span danger","threats at thandol span"},it="danger",add="a33b8b45"}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf of Ironforge, you can take pride in the Span as a masterwork of your stonemasons. Yet it is a painful battleground where Dark Iron kin have brought destruction to your doorstep.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you depend on the Span as the only direct overland link between Khaz Modan and the beleaguered northern outposts of Lordaeron. Its defense is vital to the war effort."},kw={"arathi highlands","balgaras","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","kam deepfury","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","zone:wetlands","zone:arathi","quest:631","quest:303","quest:378","npc:kam-deepfury","topic:second-war"},src={"Thandol Span"}}
E["subzone:thoradin-s-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Thoradin's Wall",z="arathi",s="At Thoradin's Wall, broken stone divides the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad Foothills. King Thoradin ordered it built long ago to shield early humanity from Amani troll incursions.",h="At Thoradin's Wall, broken stone divides the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad Foothills.",sec={{t="A Bulwark of Ancient Arathor",b="Thoradin's Wall once guarded Strom's western frontier. Nearly three thousand years ago, King Thoradin raised it across the valley corridor to shield humanity's young settlements from Amani forest troll raids. Strom stood at the heart of Arathor, the first unified human empire. The wall protected its heartland, giving humanity room to survive and challenge troll supremacy in the north.",sp=0},{t="Centuries of Decay",b="Thoradin's Wall now lies in severe disrepair. Great breaches split its ramparts, worn down by weather, warfare, and abandonment. Arathor splintered into rival kingdoms, and neighboring Lordaeron later fell to the Scourge. No central realm remains to maintain the masonry. Travelers and roaming bandits pass freely through the broken archways between Hillsbrad and the untamed Arathi Highlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built Thoradin's Wall?",a="King Thoradin commissioned Thoradin's Wall nearly three thousand years ago. He unified humanity's tribes and founded the Empire of Arathor.",al={"who made thoradins wall","creator of thoradins wall","thoradin wall origins"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the wall built in the first place?",a="King Thoradin ordered Thoradin's Wall built to defend Strom, humanity's early capital, and its fledgling settlements from raids by the neighboring Amani troll empire.",al={"purpose of thoradins wall","why build the wall","what was thoradins wall for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the wall so broken down today?",a="Thousands of years of weathering, conflict, and neglect have broken down Thoradin's Wall. After Arathor splintered into independent human nations, the frontier fortification lost its strategic priority and fell into disrepair.",al={"why is thoradin wall broken","who destroyed thoradins wall","why ruined"},it="ruin"},{q="What regions does Thoradin's Wall separate?",a="Thoradin's Wall separates the Hillsbrad Foothills to the west from the Arathi Highlands to the east.",al={"where is thoradins wall","what does the wall divide","border of thoradins wall"}},{q="What is Thoradin's Wall?",a="Thoradin's Wall is an ancient, colossal stone rampart that spans the border between the Arathi Highlands and Hillsbrad Foothills. Raised millennia ago during the height of the Empire of Arathor, it served as humanity's grand defensive bulwark to shield the heartlands around Strom from the fierce incursions of the Amani trolls. Today, though heavily weathered and broken, its towering arches and crumbling stones still loom over the trade road.",al={"what is thoradins wall","thoradin wall info","about thoradins wall"},it="place",add="b3263746"},{q="What happened at Thoradin's Wall?",a="For generations, the wall held firm against countless raids by the forest trolls of Zul'Aman, defending humanity's cradle. Over subsequent centuries, neglect, wars, and the sheer passage of time saw its defenses decay into the ruins standing today.",al={"history of thoradins wall","thoradins wall battles","what happened here"},it="history",add="a3fa6dab"},{q="Why is it called Thoradin's Wall?",a="The wall is named in honor of High King Thoradin, the legendary warlord who first unified the warring human tribes into the glorious Empire of Arathor. Shortly after establishing his empire and founding its great capital of Strom, Thoradin ordered the construction of this vast fortification to secure mankind's survival against hostile wilderness threats, ensuring his name remained etched in stone across the frontier.",al={"why is it called thoradins wall","who is thoradins wall named after","thoradin wall name"},it="name",add="bb7d6206"}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you stand before Thoradin's Wall and face human antiquity in the enduring masonry of King Thoradin, who first unified the scattered human tribes.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you see in these ruined fortifications the trace of ancient territorial wars, when humanity halted the forest trolls' domain."},kw={"amani","arathi","arathor","hillsbrad","strom","thoradin","thoradin's wall","wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:troll","topic:dwarf","topic:syndicate"},src={"Thoradin's Wall"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-arathor"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Arathor",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist ogres hold the Tower of Arathor among the ruins of Stromgarde Keep. The spire once served Archmage Trelane in the former mage district, southwest in the keep.",h="Boulderfist ogres hold the Tower of Arathor among the ruins of Stromgarde Keep.",sec={{t="A Bastion Overrun",b="In Stromgarde Keep's mage district, the spire rises above ruins and bears the name of the ancient Empire of Arathor. It once served the realm's sorcerers, most notably Archmage Trelane. He devised a magical defensive grid keyed to enchanted gemstones to guard the sanctum.\n\nAfter the Third War, the Syndicate and the Boulderfist ogre clan assaulted Stromgarde, and the kingdom fractured. Trelane tried to hold the tower with his arcane wards, but the ogres overwhelmed him. He fled the city for his life and left his most prized arcane artifacts behind. Now the Boulderfist brute Ruul Onestone and his followers hold the spire.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Lost Relics",b="Even in exile, Trelane would not abandon his life's work. He enlisted his former pupil, Archmage Malin of the Kirin Tor, and an expedition set out to retrieve his phylactery, orb, and ember agate. Working from Refuge Pointe, Malin's agents learned that the ogres had pillaged the stones needed to command the tower's automated defenses.\n\nThe agents crafted a replacement enchanted agate and placed it on the pedestals framing the tower's threshold. This awakened conjured water elementals to purge the ogre occupiers, allowing adventurers to recover Trelane's heirlooms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Arathor?",a="The Tower of Arathor rises in the southwestern ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Named for the ancient human empire of Arathor, it served as a center of study for the kingdom's mages until invading ogres took it.",al={"tower of arathor","stromgarde mage tower","arathi tower"}},{q="Who lives in the tower now?",a="Boulderfist ogres occupy the tower and the surrounding mage district. The ogre mage Ruul Onestone dwells inside the spire with his guards, who have rooted out and guarded the relics left by its former master.",al={"who is in the tower of arathor","tower of arathor mobs","tower of arathor boss"}},{q="Who was Archmage Trelane?",a="Archmage Trelane was a prominent wizard of Stromgarde who lived and studied in the tower. He created its gemstone-powered wards, then fled into exile after failing to defend the sanctum from the Boulderfist assault.",al={"archmage trelane","who owned the tower","trelane"}},{q="How do the tower's defenses work?",a="Trelane keyed the tower to awaken when an enchanted agate is placed on the pedestals flanking its entrance. The arcane matrix then conjures hostile water elementals to battle intruders occupying the entrance.",al={"how to activate tower defenses","trelane's defenses","tower pedestals"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Mage, you can see what became of Stromgarde's arcane enclave and Archmage Trelane's mastery of defensive elemental constructs.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help Archmage Malin's agents recover Trelane's lost artifacts in contested Stromgarde Keep. That denies potent magical relics to the encroaching Boulderfist clan."},kw={"arathi","boulderfist","malin","ruul onestone","skuerto","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","quest:690","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance","topic:third-war"},src={"Tower of Arathor"}}
E["subzone:witherbark-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Witherbark Village",z="arathi",s="In the southeastern Arathi Highlands, Witherbark Village shelters hostile forest trolls beside a secluded lake. The tribe raids Stromgarde's Alliance remnants and the Horde outpost at Hammerfall.",h="In the southeastern Arathi Highlands, Witherbark Village shelters hostile forest trolls beside a secluded...",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Forest Trolls",b="Witherbark trolls hold the shore and paths around their mountain lake. Fishers, axe throwers, and witch doctors live in huts along the water. Zalas Witherbark and the tribe's shadow hunters direct their people from a great cavern behind the settlement.\n\nThe Witherbark have joined forces with the Boulderfist ogres to claim more of the highlands. They have also taken a firm foothold in the ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Any outsider who enters their territory risks a fierce attack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Witherbark Village?",a="The Witherbark tribe, forest trolls native to the region, holds the settlement. Headhunters, axe throwers, fishers, and witch doctors defend the lake and its surrounding paths.",al={"who are witherbark","witherbark trolls","who controls witherbark village"}},{q="What is inside the large cave behind the village?",a="The great cavern holds the tribe's leaders. Chieftain Zalas Witherbark and the shadow hunters direct the tribe's raids and defenses from within its tunnels.",al={"witherbark cave","cave behind witherbark village","zalas witherbark location"}},{q="Why are the Witherbark trolls working with ogres?",a="The Witherbark have formed a loose alliance of convenience with the local Boulderfist ogres. Together, they can press Stromgarde's weakened human defenders and threaten rivals such as the Horde at Hammerfall.",al={"witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and boulderfist","why are trolls allied with ogres"}},{q="Are the Witherbark friendly to the Horde?",a="No. The Witherbark resent the modern Horde and its Darkspear trolls, and they fight the Horde at Hammerfall. They attack Horde travelers on sight.",al={"are witherbark horde","can horde talk to witherbark","witherbark reputation"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Witherbark give no deference to the new Horde. They often clash with scouts from Hammerfall and threaten travel through the eastern passes.",["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you will find no kinship with the Witherbark. These forest trolls regard jungle trolls and the Horde with deep hostility."},kw={"arathi highlands","forest trolls","nimar the slayer","witherbark","witherbark village","zalas witherbark"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:troll","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Witherbark Village"}}
E["zone:arathi"] = {t="zone",n="Arathi Highlands",z="arathi",s="In Arathi, ruined Stromgarde leaves the highlands at war on several fronts. The kingdom's remnants, the Horde, Syndicate nobles, and invading ogres fight for the ancient birthplace of the Empire of Arathor in southeastern Lordaeron.",h="In Arathi, ruined Stromgarde leaves the highlands at war on several fronts.",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="The dry plains of Arathi once formed the heart of a united human realm. Millennia ago, King Thoradin gathered the divided tribes beneath the Arathi banner and built their capital, Strom, on ground that was easy to defend. During the Troll Wars, humanity made its compact with the high elves here and learned the arcane arts to drive back the Amani.\n\nNoble bloodlines later spread north into Lordaeron and south toward Stormwind. The imperial guard remained and formed Stromgarde, a martial kingdom that guarded the border against forest trolls for ages.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Kingdom",b="Under King Thoras Trollbane, Stromgarde helped defend the Alliance during the Second War. The Third War and its aftermath broke the kingdom. It escaped the worst of the Scourge plague, but King Thoras's mysterious death plunged the realm into turmoil. Boulderfist ogres came down from the hills, while nobles of Alterac in the Syndicate seized wide districts of Stromgarde Keep.\n\nPrince Galen Trollbane and his loyalists now hold a small part of the city and their refuge at Refuge Pointe. Against heavy odds, they fight a bitter guerrilla war.",sp=0},{t="The War for the Highlands",b="Arathi is contested by forces with different claims. In the northeast, the Horde made Hammerfall from an abandoned human internment camp and named it for Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. The outpost anchors their northern holdings and protects their allies in Hillsbrad. The Witherbark trolls seek vengeance against the humans who once persecuted them, while the Argus Wake guides the Syndicate's occupation.\n\nAt the plateau's center, the ancient Circles of Binding hold elementals in place. They restrain an old power buried beneath the stone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Stromgarde Keep?",a="After King Thoras Trollbane died, strife engulfed Stromgarde and attackers closed in. Boulderfist ogres took the outer districts, while the Syndicate seized the keep's sanctum. Prince Galen Trollbane and his dwindling garrison hold one fortified corner and fight for their capital.",al={"why is stromgarde ruined","who controls stromgarde","stromgarde status"}},{q="What is Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is a Horde outpost built in the remains of a human internment camp where orcs were held after the Second War. Its name honors former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who died leading the campaign to free captives from camps across Lordaeron.",al={"horde base arathi","history of hammerfall","why is it called hammerfall"}},{q="Where does the Alliance operate in Arathi?",a="Alliance soldiers and Stromgarde defenders operate from Refuge Pointe, a naturally fortified canyon in the center of the highlands. From there, they attack to reclaim Stromgarde Keep and push back ogres and trolls.",al={"alliance base arathi","refuge pointe","where are the stromgarde humans"}},{q="What are the stone circles across the plains?",a="The Inner, Outer, East, and West Circles of Binding are ancient magical seals guarded and maintained by rogue elementals. They imprison an unknown, primordial being deep beneath the highlands.",al={"circles of binding","elementals in arathi","stone circles"}},{q="How do you reach the Arathi Highlands?",a="From the north and west, travelers cross the breach in Thoradin's Wall from the Hillsbrad Foothills. From Khaz Modan in the south, they cross the dwarven bridge of the Thandol Span over the chasm between the highlands and the Wetlands.",al={"getting to arathi","how to get to arathi highlands","arathi entrance"}},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in Arathi?",a="The Syndicate is made up of exiled Alteraci nobles who seek new domains by pillaging fallen realms. In Arathi, they have taken large parts of Stromgarde Keep and nearby farms, including Northfold Manor.",al={"why is syndicate in arathi","syndicate stromgarde","who leads the syndicate here"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human, you share roots with every kingdom in the Empire of Arathor. Seeing its ancient seat broken and overrun by ogres and thieves is a deep cultural loss.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Hammerfall as sacred ground. It honors Orgrim Doomhammer's sacrifice to free an enslaved people from internment.",["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you follow Stromgarde's celebrated martial tradition. Its rugged battlegrounds are a revered trial by arms.",["profession:Mining"]="As a miner, you can find iron and mithril in Arathi's craggy ridges. Drywhisker Gorge is the only known source of lesser bloodstone ore."},kw={"arathi","arathi highlands","arathor","boulderfist","galen trollbane","hammerfall","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","thoradin's wall"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:thoradin-s-wall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:hillsbrad","zone:wetlands"},src={"Arathi Highlands (Classic)","Arathi Highlands"}}
